(36, 'ABS', 'C100C01', 'Hardware fault is detected by wheel speed input circuit of the ECU.', 'General Electrical Failure', NULL, 'Damage of the wheel speed sensor wiring or connector, wheel speed sensor or its wiring shorted to ground or supply', 'Check the cables and connectors between ECU and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Disconnect wheel speed sensor from ECU. 1. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. -> Change Sensor or wiring if out of range 2. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. -> Change Sensor or wiring if out of range', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 6'),
(37, 'ABS', 'C100C25', 'If the minimum measurable wheel- speed is above its limit value, then fault is set. (Limit speed is 10 [km/h])', 'Signal Shape / Waveform Failure', NULL, 'Large airgap, dirty tone wheel, toggling tone wheel, damaged tone wheel (missing or destroyed tone wheel teeth)', 'Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3- 4km/h). Check the cables and connectors between ECU and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. If possible : Check tone wheel by checking wheel speed sensor signal for correct wave(Not possible to define the correct waveform) form according the specification for wheel speed sensor wave form or check tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth. Check wheel speed sensor mounting.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 6'),
(38, 'ABS', 'C100C29', 'ABS activation frequency on wheel is implausible', 'Signal invalid', NULL, 'Large airgap, dirty tone wheel, missing or destroyed tone wheel teeth, toggling tone wheel, production- failures of tone wheel, damaged wheel speed sensor, wheel speed sensor mounting', 'Check the tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth. Check wheel speed sensor mounting (Check Klämhylsa). Check the cables and connectors between ECU and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 ... 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Do waveform check with oscilloscope. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h).', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 6'),
(39, 'ABS', 'C100C2F', 'Plausibility test for the wheel speed sensor signal frequency (frequency jumps)', 'Signal Erratic', NULL, 'Large airgap, dirty tone wheel, missing or destroyed tone wheel teeth, toggling tone wheel, production- failures of tone wheel, damaged wheel speed sensor, wheel speed sensor mounting', 'Check the tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth. Check wheel speed sensor mounting (Check Klämhylsa). Check the cables and connectors between ECU and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 ... 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Do waveform check with oscilloscope. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h).', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 6'),
(40, 'ABS', 'C100C31', 'a not plausible drop of the wheel speed signal happens (or signal is frequently jumping between above 11[km/h] and zero), error is set.', 'No Signal', NULL, 'Damage of cables or connectors (Short circuit between H and L) Too large airgap between tone wheel and wheel speed sensor, damage of wheel speed sensor mounting, damaged or wrong tone wheel, damaged wheel speed sensor or ECU electronic circuit', 'Check the cables and connectors between ECU and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits (between H and L) and open-circuits. Measure Voltage between ECU GND and wheel speed sensor (any pin) Voltage must in range 0.5-4.3V. Disconnect wheel speed sensor from ECU. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h).', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 6'),
(41, 'ABS', 'C100C38', 'The error is set if the current wheel speed differs (>25%) from the average of the other wheels for a long time.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, 'tyre with wrong circumference is mounted, wrong tone wheel, puncture of the tyre, continuous brake force on a wheel without brake activated by ABS. Damage in the wiring and/or connectors between WSS and ECU. Undetected fault of the wheel speed sensor, too big airgap (dropped out wheel speed sensor)', 'Check tire and check the brakes. If error still active, check Wheel speed sensors by driving and monitoring. Wheel speed shall not differ more than 25 %. check tone wheel', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 6'),
(42, 'ABS', 'C100C54', 'The deviation between the learned wheel circumferences and the EOL programmed values are too large (deviation > 25%).', 'Missing Calibration', NULL, 'Tyre with wrong circumference is mounted on one of the axels, wrong calibration of C3 -signal, tachograph not calibrated, wrong parameter for wheel cirumference, number of teeth of tone wheel.', 'Check if tire size of all tires is according vehicle specification. Check C3 Signal calibration, check tachograp for additional faultcodes. Check number of teeth on tone wheel on all wheels. (Check tire size of all tires in data set.) V3P to check', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 6'),
(43, 'ABS', 'C001011', '-Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information. Resistance between the output and the vehicle ground is less then 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, 'Damage in the wiring (low resistance to ground on high side) and/or connectors between PCV and ECU, damaged PCV or ECU', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
(44, 'ABS', 'C001012', 'Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information. If the output is higher then 3 V for the duration of the detection time.', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, 'Damage in the wiring (low resistance to voltage source above 1V) and/or connectors between PCV and ECU, or damaged ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors to Inlet valve of PCV Left for short circuit to all other cables and pins (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm, voltage difference between valve and vehicle ground should be lower than 1 V. In case of lower resistance or higher voltage difference, repair wiring harness. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activat PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Left Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
(45, 'ABS', 'C001013', 'Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information. Resistance at output pin is higher than 1 kOhm.', 'Circuit Open', NULL, 'Damage in the wiring (interruption) and/or connectors between PCV and ECU, damaged PCV or ECU', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If values are not ok replace PCV, otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
