(65, 'ABS', 'C001D11', 'Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information. Resistance between the output and the vehicle ground is less then 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, 'Damage in the wiring (low resistance to ground on high side) and/or connectors between PCV and ECU, damaged PCV or ECU', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Right Rear ABS Outlet Valve'),
(66, 'ABS', 'C001D12', 'Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information. If the output is higher then 3 V for the duration of the detection time.', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, 'Damage in the wiring (low resistance to voltage source above 1V) and/or connectors between PCV and ECU, or damaged ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors to outlet valve of PCV Right for short circuit to all other cables and pins (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm, voltage difference between valve and vehicle ground should be lower than 1 V. In case of lower resistance or higher voltage difference, repair wiring harness. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activat PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Right Rear ABS Outlet Valve'),
(67, 'ABS', 'C001D13', 'Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information. Resistance at output pin is higher than 1 kOhm.', 'Circuit Open', NULL, 'Damage in the wiring (interruption) and/or connectors between PCV and ECU, damaged PCV or ECU', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If values are not ok replace PCV, otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Right Rear ABS Outlet Valve'),
(68, 'ABS', 'C10044A', 'ECU is configured for one axle valve but 2 valves are connected', 'Incorrect Component Installed', NULL, 'There is a valve connected without being configured', 'Check the configuration of the vehicle (2s2m or 2s1m on this axle). If the 2s2m is correct, correct dataset of ECU', 'Left Front ABS Valve Module'),
(69, 'ABS', 'C10054A', 'ECU is configured for one axle valve but 2 valves are connected', 'Incorrect Component Installed', NULL, 'There is a valve connected without being configured', 'Check the configuration of the vehicle (2s2m or 2s1m on this axle). If the 2s2m is correct, correct dataset of ECU', 'Right Front ABS Valve Module'),
(70, 'ABS', 'C10064A', 'ECU is configured for one axle valve but 2 valves are connected', 'Incorrect Component Installed', NULL, 'There is a valve connected without being configured', 'Check the configuration of the vehicle (2s2m or 2s1m on this axle). If the 2s2m is correct, correct dataset of ECU', 'Left Rear ABS Valve Module'),
(71, 'ABS', 'C20074A', 'ECU is configured for one axle valve but 2 valves are connected', 'Incorrect Component Installed', NULL, 'There is a valve connected without being configured', 'Check the configuration of the vehicle (2s2m or 2s1m on this axle). If the 2s2m is correct, correct dataset of ECU', 'Right Rear ABS Valve Module'),
(72, 'ABS', 'C200068', 'The error is set if not all necessary data is available for EBD- function', 'Event Information', NULL, 'brake pedal demand signal not available', 'Check brake demand pressure sensor signal components: check cable, sensor and signal range (full brake application) or permanent brake application signal (offset error)', 'Electric Brake Force Distribution'),
(73, 'ABS', 'C200163', 'Duration of ABS activity is too long or ABS brake pressure demands are low for an implausible long time. Detection time (3s-10min) depends on driving situations.', 'Circuit / Component Protection Time-Out', NULL, 'fault of at least one wheel speed sensor or its mounting, damages of at least one tone wheel, noisy wheel speed signal, wrong data in dataset, differences in tyre sizes, puncture of a tyre, continuous brake force on a wheel (dragging wheel, without brake pressure).', 'Check tyre, check pneumatic and mechanical parts of wheel brakes. Check wheel speed signal components: check cable, sensor and tone wheel. Check if configuration stored in the ECU corresponds to wheel rolling circumference and tone-wheel teeth number. If those do not conform, then correct the configuration values or change the part of the vehicle.', 'Anti-Lock Brake System'),
(74, 'ABS', 'C100E11', 'Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information. Resistance between the output and the vehicle ground is less then 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, 'Damage in the wiring (low resistance to ground on high side) and/or connectors between PCV and ECU, damaged PCV or ECU', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Additional ABS Outlet Valve'),
(75, 'ABS', 'C100E12', 'Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information. If the output is higher then 3 V for the duration of the detection time.', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, 'Damage in the wiring (low resistance to voltage source above 1V) and/or connectors between PCV and ECU, or damaged ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors to outlet valve of PCV Left for short circuit to all other cables and pins (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm, voltage difference between valve and vehicle ground should be lower than 1 V. In case of lower resistance or higher voltage difference, repair wiring harness. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activat PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Left Additional ABS Outlet Valve'),
(76, 'ABS', 'C100E13', 'Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information. Resistance at output pin is higher than 1 kOhm.', 'Circuit Open', NULL, 'Damage in the wiring (interruption) and/or connectors between PCV and ECU, damaged PCV or ECU', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If values are not ok replace PCV, otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Additional ABS Outlet Valve'),
