(995, 'DM', 'B150613', 'Open circuit conditions detected on output pin', 'Circuit Open', NULL, '1. Harness issue. 2. Actuator motor blown.', '- Inspect the Power Window Motor. - Inspect the Door seal ageing. - Inspect the harness and connectors.', 'Power Window Motor'),
(996, 'DM', 'B150618', 'Feedback load current measured on the output is lower than defined threshold. Threshold is dynamic and based on multicriteria formula (voltage, temperature and motor type).', 'Circuit Current Below Threshold', NULL, '1. Anormal window mechanical resistance, 2. Power motor issue (Thermal switch open, etc) 3. Door sealing ageing.', '- Inspect the Power Window Motor. - Inspect the Door seal ageing. - Inspect the harness and connectors.', 'Power Window Motor'),
(997, 'DM', 'B150619', 'Feedback load current measured on the output is higher than defined threshold. Threshold is dynamic and based on multicriteria formula (voltage, temperature and motor type).', 'Circuit Current Above Threshold', NULL, '1. Anormal window mechanical resistance, 2. Power motor issue, 3. Door sealing ageing.', '- Inspect the Power Window Motor. - Inspect the Door seal ageing. - Inspect the harness and connectors.', 'Power Window Motor'),
(998, 'DM', 'U114668', 'Maximum number of DTC reached: 29 DTC.', 'Event Information', NULL, '1. Unexpected environment conditions; 2. ECU failure', '- Clear all DTC.', 'DTC Notification Max Limit Reached'),
(999, 'xBS', 'U014087', 'The error is set if messages from VMCU are not comming or missing.', 'Missing Message', NULL, 'Failure is out of EAS system.', 'Failure is out of EAS system. Check ECU:s transmitting VMCU signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With VMCU'),
(1000, 'xBS', 'U300007', 'The error is set if the ECUs moisture indicator indicates too high moisture content.', 'Mechanical Failures', NULL, 'Mechanical damage of the EAS ECUs housing or damage of the EAS ECU, connector', 'Replace EAS ECU and check connector', 'Electronic control unit'),
(1001, 'xBS', 'U300041', 'Checksum error detetced in the application software', 'General Checksum Failure', NULL, 'Previously interrupted flash download, or damage of the EAS ECU (defect program memory)', 'Download update of application software, if the error is still active, replace EAS ECU.', 'Electronic control unit'),
(1002, 'xBS', 'U300044', 'The error is set if RAM error in EAS ECU is detected', 'Data Memory Failure', NULL, 'Damage of the EAS ECU (defect RAM cel)', 'Replace EAS ECU.', 'Electronic control unit'),
(1003, 'xBS', 'U300045', 'Error detected in the application software memory', 'Program Memory Failure', NULL, 'Damage of the EAS ECU (defect program memory)', 'Replace EAS ECU.', 'Electronic control unit'),
(1004, 'xBS', 'U300046', 'Error is set if incompatibilities between EEPROM dataset and drive software, hardware or bootloader versions are found, if there are unplausible data in the dataset, or if EEPROM has a failure', 'Calibration / Parameter Memory Failure', NULL, 'Main switch (power supply of ECU) was switched off while EAS afterrun, incorrect data in the dataset, dataset inconsistent to ECU, damaged EAS ECU (EEPROM)', 'Download update of application software, if the error is still active, replace EAS ECU.', 'Electronic control unit'),
(1005, 'xBS', 'U300049', 'An ECU self monitoring function detected an ECU hardware failure', 'Internal Electronic Failure', NULL, 'Damage of EAS ECU', 'Replace EAS ECU.', 'Electronic control unit'),
(1006, 'xBS', 'U30004B', 'Temperature monitoring is carried out by reading the hardware status information of the ECU.', 'Over Temperature', NULL, 'Ambient temperature too high or damage of the EAS ECU', 'Check ECU location and suroundings for high temperatures. - If fault is active, replace it.', 'Electronic control unit'),
(1007, 'xBS', 'U300094', 'An ECU plausibility monitoring function detected an ECU hardware failure', 'Unexpected Operation', NULL, 'Damage of EAS ECU', 'Replace EAS ECU', 'Electronic control unit'),
(1008, 'xBS', 'U300096', 'The error is set if not safety critical components of the ECU are damaged', 'Component Internal Failure', NULL, 'Damage of the EAS ECU', 'Replace EAS ECU', 'Electronic control unit'),
(1009, 'xBS', 'U002888', 'The error is set if Chassis CAN is in bus off status.', 'Bus off', NULL, 'Damaged Chassis CAN network wiring and/or connectors (e.g. short circuit), electro-magnetic disturbance, damaged EAS ECU, other damaged Chassis CAN ECUs', 'Check the cables and connectors and wiring nodes between other Chassis CAN ECUs and EAS ECU. Check for sufficient power supply. If no fault found, check if no disturbing improper devices are mounted. If error still active check with other chassis CAN ECUs. If error still active check with other EAS ECU.', 'CAN Communication Chassis Net'),
(1010, 'xBS', 'U300316', 'Failure is set if supply voltage of the EAS ECU is out of range (supply voltage is equal or lower than 15V).', 'Circuit Voltage Below Threshold', NULL, 'Battery is not charged enough or damage of the vehicles power supply system, or damage in the wiring or connectors for the EAS ECU supply', 'If the state is active continuously, check vehicles power supply system and voltage supply wiring to ECU.', 'Battery Power'),
(1011, 'xBS', 'U300317', 'Failure is set if supply voltage of the EAS ECU is out of range (supply voltage is equal or higher than 36V).', 'Circuit Voltage Above Threshold', NULL, 'Damage of the vehicles power supply system', 'If the state is active continuously, check vehicles power supply system.', 'Battery Power'),
(1012, 'xBS', 'U30031C', 'Failure is set if supply voltage of the EAS ECU is out of range (supply voltage is out of [19.5 ... 32]V).', 'Circuit Voltage Out of Range', NULL, 'Battery is not charged enough or damage of the vehicles power supply system, or damage in the wiring or connectors for the EAS ECU supply', 'If the state is active continuously, check vehicles power supply system and voltage supply wiring to ECU.', 'Battery Power'),
(1013, 'xBS', 'C005122', 'The failure is reported if the sensor signal exceeds the maximum possible range of the steering wheel angle set by EoL-parameter.', 'Signal Amplitude Greater Than Maximum', NULL, 'Sensor is calibrated or mounted wrongly or steering system does not correspond to the vehicle specification (wrong steering gearbox or steering gear arm) or wrong maximum parameter in dataset or steering wheel angle sensor damaged.', 'Check if sensor is calibrated correctly: with engine running, set steered wheels in straight position, read steering angle via diagnosis, check if the value of steering angle is 0 +- 10 degrees. If value is not OK, recalibrate the sensor. While engine still running, mark zero position on the steering wheel and turn it in both directions by one turn (360 degrees). Check the steering angle values via diagnosis (+-360 degrees). If values are not OK, check the mounting and the drive of the sensor. If fault is still active check steering system for specified parts (e.g. steering lever). With engine running turn the steering wheel to its end positions, read the steering angle values via diagnosis and check if the read values are within the allowed range defined in the dataset. If fault is still active, replace the steering angle sensor.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1014, 'xBS', 'C005127', 'The failure is reported, if the steering angle sensor signal changes too fast.', 'Signal Rate of Change Above Threshold', NULL, 'Mounting or drive of the sensor defect or sensor defect.', 'Check the mounting and the drive of the sensor. If fault still active, replace the steering angle sensor.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1015, 'xBS', 'C005128', 'The failure is reported if the offset of the steering angle sensor is higher than 90 degrees (depending on dataset parameter) or if the fast offset adjustment of the sensor (started via diagnosis) results in a high offset (90 degrees depending on dataset parameter).', 'Signal Bias Level Out of Range / Zero Adjustment Failure', NULL, 'Sensor is calibrated or mounted wrongly or wrong parameter for threshold in dataset or steering angle sensor is damaged.', 'Check the mounting of the sensor and check if sensor is calibrated correctly (+-10 degree in straight line position). If necessary recalibrate the sensor. If fault is still active check steering system for specified parts. If fault is still active, replace the steering angle sensor.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1016, 'xBS', 'C005149', 'The steering angle sensor has an internal supervision which monitors the operation of the sensor and indicates its status via CAN- Sensor. The EAS ECU monitors the sensor status flags and the range of the sensor values.', 'Internal Electronic Failure', NULL, 'Internal sensor error', 'Replace the steering angle sensor.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1017, 'xBS', 'C005154', 'This failure is reported if the End Of Line Calibration of the steering angle sensor is not finished. (SAS fast adjustment calibration routine has not been started).', 'Missing Calibration', NULL, 'ECU or SAS was replaced or initial dataset reloaded.', 'Recalibrate the steering angle sensor. (Start fast adjustment routine)', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1018, 'xBS', 'C005155', 'This failure is reported if a steering angle sensor is detected, however it is not configured.', 'Not Configured', NULL, 'Installed but not configured (in ECU) component', 'Check if configuration matches installation. Download correct dataset.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1019, 'xBS', 'C005161', 'Not calibrated status of the steering angle sensor is detected by the EAS ECU.', 'Signal Calculation Failure', NULL, 'New steering angle sensor was mounted or steering angle sensor was reset or calibration of steering angle sensor was not successful or sensor unit is damaged or EAS ECU is damaged', 'Calibrate the sensor again. If calibration cannot be performed successfully, check with an other sensor. If it still not possible to calibrate the sensor, check with other ECU.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1020, 'xBS', 'C005176', 'The failure is reported, if the sign of the steering angle sensor signal is incorrect.', 'Wrong Mounting Position', NULL, 'Sensor is mounted wrongly or the steering angle sensor is damaged.', 'While engine still running, mark zero position on the steering wheel and turn it in both directions by one turn (360 degrees). Check the steering angle sign values via diagnosis (+-360 degrees, sign should be negative while turning left and positive while turning right). If values are not OK, check the mounting and the drive of the sensor. If fault is still active check steering system for specified parts (e.g. steering lever). With engine running turn the steering wheel to its end positions, read the steering angle values via diagnosis and check if the read values are within the allowed range defined in the dataset. If fault is still active, replace the steering angle sensor.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1021, 'xBS', 'C005193', 'The failure is reported if after a vehicle standstill a left and a right curve has been detected, but the steering angle sensor signal has not changed.', 'No Operation', NULL, 'Sensor is mounted wrongly or the steering angle sensor is damaged.', 'Check correct mounting or damages of the sensor. If mounting is OK, then replce the sensor.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1022, 'xBS', 'U012687', 'The error is set if the EAS ECU does not receive any messages from the steering angle sensor.', 'Missing Message', NULL, 'Damaged wiring and/or connectors between steering angle sensor and EAS ECU steering angle sensor is not connected to the EAS ECU, damaged steering angle sensor, damaged EAS ECU.', 'Check the wiring and connectors between steering angle sensor and EAS ECU and external yaw rate sensor and EAS ECU for open circuit and physical damage (including check for chafing damage), check the power supply of the ESP sensors 8,3V - 14,5V, if error still active, replace steering angle sensor, if error still active, replace EAS ECU.', 'Lost Communication With Steering Angle Sensor Module'),
(1023, 'xBS', 'C100C01', 'The 12V voltage and the current of Steering Angle sensor supply are monitored (hardware feedback signals on central ECU). The error is set if there is a parasitic voltage greater then - Above 4.5V before switching ON sensor supply - Overcurrent is detected during normal operation (200-600 mA). - External sensor sends voltage error information.', 'General Electrical Failure', NULL, 'Damage of the Steering Angle sensor wiring or connectors, or damage of the central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and Steering Angle sensor for short-circuits. 1. Remove sensor and check for faultcodes again. 2. If still a problem with sensors removed the problem is in the harness or ECU. 3. Check wiring for shortcuts to ground or other signals and CNT (below 3 ohm). Repair if faulty 4. If harness is ok and there is still active faultcode, replace ECU. 5. If harness is ok and no active fault try to move harness to reproduce the fault.', 'EBS ESP Sensor Supply'),
(1024, 'xBS', 'C100C16', 'The error is set, if the Steering Angle sensor supply voltage is lower than the working limit (8.3 [V]).', 'Circuit Voltage Below Threshold', NULL, 'Damage of the Steering Angle sensor wiring or connectors, or damage of the central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and Steering Angle sensor for short-circuits. If error is still active replace central ECU.', 'EBS ESP Sensor Supply'),
(1025, 'xBS', 'C100C17', 'The error is set, if the Steering Angle Sensor supply voltage is higher than the working limit (14.5 [V]).', 'Circuit Voltage Above Threshold', NULL, 'Damage of the Steering Angle sensor wiring or connectors, damage of the central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and Steering Angle sensor for short-circuits to other signals higher than 12 V. If error is still active replace central ECU.', 'EBS ESP Sensor Supply'),
(1026, 'xBS', 'C100C49', 'Hardware test is performed and feedback is monitored.', 'Internal Electronic Failure', NULL, 'Damaged central ECU', 'Replace central ECU', 'EBS ESP Sensor Supply'),
(1027, 'xBS', 'U012987', 'The error is set if messages from brakes are not coming or missing.', 'Missing Message', NULL, 'Failure is out of EAS system.', 'Failure is out of EAS system. Check ECU:s transmitting EBS signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With Brake System Control Module'),
(1028, 'xBS', 'U116968', 'The error is set if the number of DTCs to be sent to diagnostics fault status message exceeds 29.', 'Event Information', NULL, 'Over 29 different faults set', 'Failure is out of EAS system. Check ECU:s transmitting EBS signals and connected components.', 'DTC Notification Max Limit Reached'),
(1029, 'xBS', 'U116A68', 'CRC or message counter error in external Steering Angle Sensor messages.', 'Event Information', NULL, 'Failure is out of EAS system.', 'Failure is out of EAS system.', 'Steering Angle Sensor Message Checksum'),
(1030, 'xBS', 'C100811', 'Error is set if the steering angle sensor supply can not be switched on or no valid supply voltage for the steering angle sensor is available during switched on. The supply voltage is less than 4.75V measured on the ECU pin.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between steering angle sensor and central ECU, damaged sterring angle sensor, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and rear axle steering angle sensor for short-circuits. The insulation resistance should be higher than 200kOhm. Disconnect the sensor, switch the ECU to After Market mode and measure the voltage of the sensor supply. If its lower than 4.8V then replace the central ECU else replace rear axle steering angle sensor.', 'Rear Active Steering Angle Sensor'),
(1031, 'xBS', 'C100816', 'Error is set if any of the two rear sensors signal voltages is less than 0.2V.', 'Circuit Voltage Below Threshold', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between steering angle sensor and central ECU, damaged sterring angle sensor, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and steering angle sensor signal for short-circuits and open-circuits.The insulation resistance should be higher than 200 kOhm and the wire resistance should be less than 5 Ohm. Switch the ECU to After Market mode and measure the voltage of the sensor signal. If its lower than 0.4V (end of line parameter) then replace rear axle steering angle sensor else replace the central ECU.', 'Rear Active Steering Angle Sensor'),
(1032, 'xBS', 'C100817', 'Error is set if any of the two rear sensors voltage is more than 4.8V', 'Circuit Voltage Above Threshold', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between steering angle sensor and central ECU, damaged sterring angle sensor, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and steering angle sensor signal for short-circuits.The insulation resistance should be higher than 200 kOhm. Switch the ECU to After Market mode and measure the voltage of the sensor signal. If its higher than 4.6V (end of line parameter) then replace rear axle steering angle sensor else replace the central ECU.', 'Rear Active Steering Angle Sensor');
INSERT INTO `dtc_list` (`id`, `node`, `dtc_iso`, `failure_event`, `ftb_name`, `funct_behavior_desc`, `possible_root_cause`, `workshop_action`, `proprietary_name`) VALUES
(1033, 'xBS', 'C10081C', 'Error is set if sum of the rear sensors voltage less than 4.7V or greater than 5.3V', 'Circuit Voltage Out of Range', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between steering angle sensor and central ECU, damaged sterring angle sensor, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and steering angle sensor signal for short-circuits and open-circuits. The insulation resistance should be higher than 200 kOhm and the wire resistance should be less than 5 Ohm. If the error is not active, then the axle must turn between the 2 end positions (by diagnostics) while the sensor voltages are measured. If the error is continuously active then switch the ECU to After Market mode and measure the voltage of both sensor signals. If sum of the signals is lower than 4.8V (end of line parameter) or higher than 5.2 then replace rear axle steering angle sensor else replace the central ECU (only if the error is continuously present and the sum of the sensor voltages measured by external tool is correct).', 'Rear Active Steering Angle Sensor'),
(1034, 'xBS', 'C100854', 'Error is set if the steering angle sensor offset is not calibrated.', 'Missing Calibration', NULL, 'Sensor is not calibrated.', 'Calibrate sensor, if not succesful reset the sensor with the diagnostic tool, and then calibrate it again. If calibration cannot be performed successfully, check mechanical parts, specs and other active failures. If error still active replace the sensor.', 'Rear Active Steering Angle Sensor'),
(1035, 'xBS', 'C100911', 'The error is set if status feedback does not correspond to the actual valve high state.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between proportional valve and central ECU, damaged proportional valve, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and proportional valve for short-circuits. The insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm. If the resistance of the proportional valve is lower than 20 Ohm replace the proportional valve. If error is still active replace the central ECU.', 'Rear Active Steering Proportional Valve A'),
(1036, 'xBS', 'C100915', 'The error is set if status feedback does not correspond to the actual valve low state.', 'Circuit Short To Battery or Open', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between proportional valve and central ECU, damaged proportional valve, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and proportional valve for short-circuits and for open circuit. The insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm and the wire resistance should be less than 3 Ohm. If the resistance of the proportional valve is higher than 30 Ohm replace the proportional valve. If error is still active replace the central ECU.', 'Rear Active Steering Proportional Valve A'),
(1037, 'xBS', 'C100A11', 'The error is set if status feedback does not correspond to the actual valve high state.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between proportional valve and central ECU, damaged proportional valve, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and proportional valve for short-circuits. The insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm. If the resistance of the proportional valve is lower than 20 Ohm replace the proportional valve. If error is still active replace the central ECU.', 'Rear Active Steering Propotional Valve B'),
(1038, 'xBS', 'C100A15', 'The error is set if status feedback does not correspond to the actual valve low state.', 'Circuit Short To Battery or Open', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between proportional valve and central ECU, damaged proportional valve, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and proportional valve for short-circuits and for open circuit. The insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm and the wire resistance should be less than 3 Ohm. If the resistance of the proportional valve is higher than 30 Ohm replace the proportional valve. If error is still active replace the central ECU.', 'Rear Active Steering Propotional Valve B'),
(1039, 'xBS', 'C100B11', 'The error is set if status feedback does not correspond to the actual valve high state.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between cut-off valve and central ECU, damaged cut-off valve, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and cutoff valve for short-circuits. The insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm. If the resistance of the cutoff valve is lower than 18 Ohm replace the cutoff valve. If error is still active replace the central ECU.', 'Rear Active Steering Cutoff Valve'),
(1040, 'xBS', 'C100B15', 'The error is set if status feedback does not correspond to the actual valve low state.', 'Circuit Short To Battery or Open', NULL, 'Damage of the wiring or connector between cut-off valve and central ECU, damaged cut-off valve, damaged central ECU', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and cutoff valve for short-circuits and for open circuit. The insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm and the wire resistance should be less than 3 Ohm. If the resistance of the cutoff valve is higher than 28 Ohm replace the cutoff valve. If error is still active replace the central ECU.', 'Rear Active Steering Cutoff Valve'),
(1041, 'xBS', 'C100B71', 'The error is set if the angle moves more than 2 degrees (end of line parameter) during a test where the cutoff valve is opened and a taget value is requested.', 'Actuator Stuck', NULL, 'Valve is stuck in closed position', 'Replace hydraulic valve', 'Rear Active Steering Cutoff Valve'),
(1042, 'xBS', 'C109B68', 'Fault is set if one of the external CAN input signals of RASec is not available or the signal indicates an error: - RearAxleSteeringFun ctionDisable (RAS switch status) - EngineSpeed - WheelBasedVehicleS peed (TACHO speed) - PusherAxleLoad - TagAxleLoad - LiftAxle1Position - LiftAxle2Position', 'Event Information', NULL, 'Disturbed CAN communication, faulty other component, faulty other ECU (outside of the EBS ECU)', 'Check other ECUs for related fault codes', 'Rear Active Steering Function'),
(1043, 'xBS', 'C108B02', 'The error is set if the difference between the calibrated vehicle speed and mean drive axle wheelspeed is higher than 20 km/h (EOL parameter)', 'General Signal Failure', NULL, 'Incorrect calibration of vehicle speed, wheel speed sensor failure', 'Check other related fault codes. Check tyre sizes of the driven wheels. If tyre sizes are correct, check tachosignal (according to regulations). If tachosignal is not correct, check components related to tachometer.', 'Rear Active Steering Inter Axle Vehicle Speed'),
(1044, 'xBS', 'C108A01', 'The error is set if the compensation offset gets higher than 2 degrees (EOL parameter)', 'General Electrical Failure', NULL, 'Incorrect wheel alignment, rear axle angle sensor value drift', 'Align wheels and recalibrate', 'Rear Active Steering Rear Angle'),
(1045, 'xBS', 'C108A64', 'The error is set if rear steering angle is too high (EOL parameter)', 'Signal Plausibility Failure', NULL, 'ECU failure', 'Replace ECU', 'Rear Active Steering Rear Angle'),
(1046, 'xBS', 'C108A77', 'The error is set if the angle is deviating too much from the target lower or higher than expected. The accepted deviation between angle and target is defined by an EOL characteristics.', 'Commanded Position Not Reachable', NULL, 'Any hydraulic failure in the vehicle (low hydraulic oil level, hydraulic pump) or hydraulic valve/cylinder failure', 'Check hydraulic oil level, check hydraulic pump, check hydraulic valve/cylinder', 'Rear Active Steering Rear Angle'),
(1047, 'xBS', 'C108964', 'The error is set if both proportional valves are activated at the same time', 'Signal Plausibility Failure', NULL, 'ECU failure', 'Replace ECU', 'Rear Active Steering Control Valves'),
(1048, 'xBS', 'C102C11', 'Internal valve short to ground.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, 'EPM damaged', 'Replace EPM, There is no meassuer to be done, the DTC is set in the EPM and send over the information to the EBS ECU. The error is also stored in the EPM.', 'Wheel 2 EPM Outlet Solenoid'),
