(1185, 'xBS', 'C107B71', '- At beginning of braking the EPMs of one axle are switched in backup- mode: Backup pressure < pressure level dependent on FBM stroke. - At end of braking the EPM is switched to backup-mode: Exhaust performance is not sufficient.', 'Actuator Stuck', NULL, '- Silencer plugged in EPM or FBM - Pneumatic pipes between FBM and EPM open or plugged - FBM damaged (mechanic/pneumatic part) - Received supply pressure values from APM incorrect - EPM damaged', 'Check backup piping between FBM and EPM. If there is no problem with pneumatic piping and silencer: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut- off pressure). Drive the system to backup via diagnostics. Measure backup pressure and pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. Apply brake pedal until ca. 2 bar is reached. If difference between the two externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5% then EPM should also be replaced. Otherwise, if DTC is still active, replace FBM. Release brake pedal fast. If backup pressure is greater than 0.3 bar 1 s after releasing brake pedal then check FBM silencer. If FBM silencer is OK, then FBM should be replaced. If backup pressure is less than 0.3 bar 1 s after releasing brake pedal but pressure in the brake chamber is still greater than 0.3 bar, then check EPM silencer. If EPM silencer is OK, then EPM should be replaced.', 'Wheel 8 EPM Pressure Control'),
(1186, 'xBS', 'C107B72', 'Difference between pressure measured by EPM and demanded pressure > 1.5 bar', 'Actuator Stuck Open', NULL, '- Silencer plugged in EPM or FBM - EPM Damaged - FBM damaged - Residual backup pressure between FBM and EPM', 'Check pneumatic piping between FBM and EPM. Check silencer. Check components for possible leakages (mainly FBM). If not problem was seen: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics to 8 bar, and then control pressure from 8 to 1 bar in 1 step. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If pressure is greater than 1.5 bar 1 s after reducing demand pressure to 1 bar, then check EPM silencer. If EPM silencer is OK then EPM should be replaced. Drive the system to backup via diagnostics. Measure backup pressure and pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. Apply brake pedal until ca. 2 bar is reached then release brake pedal fast. If backup pressure is greater than 0.3 bar 1 s after releasing brake pedal then check FBM silencer. If FBM silencer is OK, then FBM should be replaced. If backup pressure is less than 0.3 bar 1 s after releasing brake pedal but pressure in the brake chamber is still greater than 0.3 bar, then check EPM silencer. If EPM silencer is OK, then EPM should be replaced.', 'Wheel 8 EPM Pressure Control'),
(1187, 'xBS', 'C107B73', '- Difference between pressure measured by EPM and demanded pressure > 1.5 bar - Pressure sensor signal> 2 bar when applying full brake. - Pressure sensor signal remains < demanded pressure and supply pressure during inlet valve protection mode of the EPM pressure control.', 'Actuator Stuck Closed', NULL, '- Damaged piping or part between EPM and wheel brake - Damaged piping or part between EPM and supply pressure - Received supply pressure values from APM incorrect - EPM damaged', 'Check pneumatic piping between EPM and supply pressure, between EPM and brake chamber. Check piping and components for possible leakages. If not problem was seen: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Measure pressure in supply reservoir and compare with read out pressure from APM via diagsnotics. Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics increased from 0 to 8 bar with 1 bar steps. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. If difference between pressure demanded by diagnostics and value read by diagnostics is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced.', 'Wheel 8 EPM Pressure Control'),
(1188, 'xBS', 'C107C29', 'Difference between measured full pressure and supply pressure > 2.2 bar', 'Signal invalid', NULL, '- Damaged or plugged piping from pressure supply to EPM - Damaged or open piping from EPM to PCV - Received supply pressure values from APM incorrect - EPM damage - PCV damage', 'Check pneumatic piping between EPM and supply pressure, and between EPM and brake chamber. Check silencer. Check piping and components for possible leakages. If not problem was seen: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Control maximum pressure at the corresponding EPM via diagnostics. Read pressure value via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. Compare the two pressure values with each other and with the defined nominal maximal braking pressure. If measured pressures are smaller than (nominal maximal braking pressure - 1bar), then EPM should be replaced. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should also be replaced.', 'Wheel 9 EPM Pressure Control'),
(1189, 'xBS', 'C107C62', 'Difference between right and left on on axle > 0.8 bar (Axles with 2 independent channels are monitored)', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '- Silencer plugged, - Damaged pneumatic pipe (leakage) between EPM and wheel brake - EPM damaged - Damaged pneumatic pipe between EPM and supply pressure if 2x1CH is used for one axle.', 'Check pneumatic piping between EPM and supply pressure (only for 2x1CH on same axle), and between EPM and brake chamber. Check silencer. Check piping and components for possible leakages. If not problem was seen: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at either EPM on the corresponding axle via diagnostics increased from 0 to 8 bar with 1 bar steps. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. If difference between pressure demaned by diagnostics and value read by diagnostics is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. Make the same test with the other EPM on the axle.', 'Wheel 9 EPM Pressure Control'),
