(1200, 'xBS', 'C107D72', 'Difference between pressure measured by EPM and demanded pressure > 1.5 bar', 'Actuator Stuck Open', NULL, '- Silencer plugged in EPM or FBM - EPM Damaged - FBM damaged - Residual backup pressure between FBM and EPM', 'Check pneumatic piping between FBM and EPM. Check silencer. Check components for possible leakages (mainly FBM). If not problem was seen: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics to 8 bar, and then control pressure from 8 to 1 bar in 1 step. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If pressure is greater than 1.5 bar 1 s after reducing demand pressure to 1 bar, then check EPM silencer. If EPM silencer is OK then EPM should be replaced. Drive the system to backup via diagnostics. Measure backup pressure and pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. Apply brake pedal until ca. 2 bar is reached then release brake pedal fast. If backup pressure is greater than 0.3 bar 1 s after releasing brake pedal then check FBM silencer. If FBM silencer is OK, then FBM should be replaced. If backup pressure is less than 0.3 bar 1 s after releasing brake pedal but pressure in the brake chamber is still greater than 0.3 bar, then check EPM silencer. If EPM silencer is OK, then EPM should be replaced.', 'Wheel 10 EPM Pressure Control'),
(1201, 'xBS', 'C107D73', '- Difference between pressure measured by EPM and demanded pressure > 1.5 bar - Pressure sensor signal> 2 bar when applying full brake. - Pressure sensor signal remains < demanded pressure and supply pressure during inlet valve protection mode of the EPM pressure control.', 'Actuator Stuck Closed', NULL, '- Damaged piping or part between EPM and wheel brake - Damaged piping or part between EPM and supply pressure - Received supply pressure values from APM incorrect - EPM damaged', 'Check pneumatic piping between EPM and supply pressure, between EPM and brake chamber. Check piping and components for possible leakages. If not problem was seen: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Measure pressure in supply reservoir and compare with read out pressure from APM via diagsnotics. Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics increased from 0 to 8 bar with 1 bar steps. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. If difference between pressure demanded by diagnostics and value read by diagnostics is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced.', 'Wheel 10 EPM Pressure Control'),
(1202, 'xBS', 'C105D11', 'Supply voltage < 4V', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check if generator diode is defect according to the manual of the generator. Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to the corresponding EPM (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. If no error found, disconnect EPM from central ECU, Wiring isolation resistances between EPM supply line and EPM ground line and between EPM supply line and vehicle ground should be above 500 Ohm. If this is not the case, disconnet supply connector from EPM, and repeat previous meauserement. If measurement is OK, then replace EPM, otherwise repair cabling. If isolation resistance with cables connected to EPM are above the limit of 500 Ohm recheck faultpresent if DTC still active then replace central ECU.', 'Wheel 1 EPM Power Supply'),
(1203, 'xBS', 'C105D12', 'Supply voltage > 4V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) (Exclude ShortCut between EPM supply.) - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to the corresponding EPM (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits to other voltage source. Drive the system to full backup via diagnostics service, then disconect EPM supply from central ECU(Meassuer at the pin of the ECU), and measure EPM supply voltage output of central ECU. If voltage is higher than 4V then replace central ECU, otherwise repair wiring harness.', 'Wheel 1 EPM Power Supply'),
(1204, 'xBS', 'C105D1B', 'Implausible voltage drop during valve activation', 'Circuit Resistance Above Threshold', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to the corresponding EPM for too high resistance. Resistance of supply wires disconnected from both central ECU and EPM should be below 3 Ohm. Check connectors for corrosion.', 'Wheel 1 EPM Power Supply'),
(1205, 'xBS', 'C105D95', 'Supply voltage of a switched-off EPM > 4V, while this EPM is switched off and another is switched on..', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) (Short curcuit between EPM supplies)', 'Get the same failure for the other EPM from the fault storage. Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to both effected EPM:s (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits between each other, and repair wiring or connector.', 'Wheel 1 EPM Power Supply'),
(1206, 'xBS', 'C105E11', 'Supply voltage < 4V', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check if generator diode is defect according to the manual of the generator. Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to the corresponding EPM (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. If no error found, disconnect EPM from central ECU, Wiring isolation resistances between EPM supply line and EPM ground line and between EPM supply line and vehicle ground should be above 500 Ohm. If this is not the case, disconnet supply connector from EPM, and repeat previous meauserement. If measurement is OK, then replace EPM, otherwise repair cabling. If isolation resistance with cables connected to EPM are above the limit of 500 Ohm recheck faultpresent if DTC still active then replace central ECU.', 'Wheel 2 EPM Power Supply'),
