(1220, 'xBS', 'C10611B', 'Implausible voltage drop during valve activation', 'Circuit Resistance Above Threshold', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to the corresponding EPM for too high resistance. Resistance of supply wires disconnected from both central ECU and EPM should be below 3 Ohm. Check connectors for corrosion.', 'Wheel 5 EPM Power Supply'),
(1221, 'xBS', 'C106195', 'Supply voltage of a switched-off EPM > 4V, while this EPM is switched off and another is switched on.', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) (Short curcuit between EPM supplies)', 'Get the same failure for the other EPM from the fault storage. Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to both effected EPM:s (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits between each other, and repair wiring or connector.', 'Wheel 5 EPM Power Supply'),
(1222, 'xBS', 'C106211', 'Supply voltage < 4V', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check if generator diode is defect according to the manual of the generator. Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to the corresponding EPM (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. If no error found, disconnect EPM from central ECU, Wiring isolation resistances between EPM supply line and EPM ground line and between EPM supply line and vehicle ground should be above 500 Ohm. If this is not the case, disconnet supply connector from EPM, and repeat previous meauserement. If measurement is OK, then replace EPM, otherwise repair cabling. If isolation resistance with cables connected to EPM are above the limit of 500 Ohm recheck faultpresent if DTC still active then replace central ECU.', 'Wheel 6 EPM Power Supply'),
(1223, 'xBS', 'C106212', 'Supply voltage > 4V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) (Exclude ShortCut between EPM supply.) - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to the corresponding EPM (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits to other voltage source. Drive the system to full backup via diagnostics service, then disconect EPM supply from central ECU(Meassuer at the pin of the ECU), and measure EPM supply voltage output of central ECU. If voltage is higher than 4V then replace central ECU, otherwise repair wiring harness.', 'Wheel 6 EPM Power Supply'),
(1224, 'xBS', 'C10621B', 'Implausible voltage drop during valve activation', 'Circuit Resistance Above Threshold', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from central ECU to the corresponding EPM for too high resistance. Resistance of supply wires disconnected from both central ECU and EPM should be below 3 Ohm. Check connectors for corrosion.', 'Wheel 6 EPM Power Supply'),
