(1330, 'xBS', 'C10704A', '- ECU receives negative or incorrect response from an EPM upon the configuration check or configuration download messages - ECU detects incompatible EPM software parts.', 'Incorrect Component Installed', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Download software update to the EPM. If error is still active(if occurnce counter is higher then 2) and error is stored only for one EPM, replace the EPM. If error is active (if occurnce counter is higher then 2) reported for every EPM, If newer SW in Central system do SWDL, if error still occuer replace central ECU.', 'Wheel 10 EPM'),
(1331, 'xBS', 'C107094', '- Fault code received from the EPM does not match to any of the defined error code registered in the central ECU - EPM does not fulfill a required test task from the central ECU - Mismatches between EPM Bootloader, drive software and hardware - Difference in voltage measured by central ECUs and EPMs > 3V.', 'Unexpected Operation', NULL, '- EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Download software update to the EPM. If error is still active(if occurnce counter is higher then 2) and error is stored only for one EPM, replace the EPM. If error is active (if occurnce counter is higher then 2) reported for every EPM, If newer SW in Central system do SWDL, if error still occuer replace central ECU.', 'Wheel 10 EPM'),
(1332, 'xBS', 'C100411', 'Resistance between vehicle ground and PCV ground < 20 kOhm..', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Pressure Control Valve Ground Circuit'),
(1333, 'xBS', 'C100412', '- Short to battery on all configured PCV outputs at the same time', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cable of the PCV ground and the cables and connectors to all installed PCV for short circuit to other wires (including check for chafing damage). Repair if faulty. If fault is still active, disconnect PCVs from the central ECU. Measure voltage on the connector between the wires of the PCVs and the vehicle ground. If the voltage is higher than 1V, repair the wiring harness. Otherwise measure the resistance between the PCV ground and the vehicle ground. If the resistance is lower than 200 kOhm, repair the wiring harness. Otherwise replace the central ECU.', 'Pressure Control Valve Ground Circuit'),
(1334, 'xBS', 'C100555', 'Valve (resistance to ground < 10kOhm) is detected, but not configured.', 'Not Configured', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Installed but not configured component', 'Check if configuration matches installation. If configuration matches installation, check the connector. If no fault is found with the connector, then check the wiring (including check for chafing damage), and repair if faulty. Insulation resistance of wiring (of the inlet and the outlet valve) towards vehicle and PCV ground must be higher than 200 kOhm.', 'Pressure Control Valve'),
(1335, 'xBS', 'C100592', '- Faulty ECU internal PCV test circuit - Short circuit to low voltage signal or weak short (50Ohm- 1kOhm) circuit to battery.', 'Performance or Incorrect Operation', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - ECU damaged', 'Check for other fault codes (also in other systems) and repair them. Erase fault codes and re-check the fault code. If error is still active, progress with the other actions. Check the wiring and connectors. Repair if faulty. Disconnect the wires from the central ECU. Measure resistance of PCV lines against the other signals of the connector. If any resistance is lower than 200 kOhm, then repair the faulty wires. Otherwise measure resistance between the ground of both PCVs and the vehicle ground. If all resistances are higher than 200 kOhm, then replace the central ECU. Else disconnect the wires also from the PCVs and measure resistance between the ground wires of both PCVs and the vehicle ground. If resistance is lower than 200 kOhm, then repair the faulty wires. If fault is still active, replace the central ECU.', 'Pressure Control Valve'),
(1336, 'xBS', 'C100616', 'Voltage < 4 V', 'Circuit Voltage Below Threshold', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and TCM (including check for chafing damage). Disconnect central ECU and TCM. Check the cables and connectors for the pressure sensor for short cuts and interruptions, resistance of TCM supply and pressure sensor supply should be less than 3 Ohm. If higher then there is an interruption on wire. Resistance between pressure sensor supply connection and all wires of different components on the same connector and to vehicle ground should be larger than 200 kOhm. If no fault is found, then replug cable again, activate Aftermarket diagnostic mode and check the voltages between the ECU pins (Voltage of TCM supply should be in range [UB - 3V ... UB + 3V]. Voltage difference should be in range [4.5 ... 5.5] V between TCM sensor supply and sensor ground.). If the measured voltages are not in the given range replace TCM. If there a still an active fault (same fault code), replace the ECU.', 'Trailer Control Modulator pressure sensor supply circuit'),
(1337, 'xBS', 'C100617', 'Voltage > 6 V', 'Circuit Voltage Above Threshold', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and TCM (including check for chafing damage). Activate AM mode. Disconnect TCM (on TCM side) and measure sensor supply wire harness to vehicle ground. Voltage should be below 1V. If above repair wire harness. Fault trace by resistance between pressure sensor supply connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm. If the voltage is below 1V then connect TCM and measure again. If higher then 6 V replace TCM. If no fault is found, then replug cable again, activate Aftermarket diagnostic mode and check the voltages between the ECU pins (Voltage of TCM supply should be in range [UB - 3V ... UB + 3V]. Voltage difference should be in range [4.5 ... 5.5] V between TCM sensor supply and sensor ground.). If there a still an active fault (same fault code), replace the ECU. If there is no active fault code try to move the harness to reproduce the fault.', 'Trailer Control Modulator pressure sensor supply circuit'),
(1338, 'xBS', 'C100021', 'Sensor signal voltage < 0.3V.', 'Signal Amplitude Less Than Minimum', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and TCM. Disconnect connector on TCM side and ECU side. Measure insulation resistance between ground (vehicle-GND and TCM-sensor GND) and signal sensor line. Resistance must be higher then 200kOhm. If it is lower then repair wiring harness. If it is not lower then connect both connectors set the ECU to After market mode via diagnosis and measure sensor signal line voltage (on TCM side). If voltage is higher then 0.4V then TCM is OK (then go to A). If not change TCM. A. Measure sensor signal voltage on ECU side. If it is higher then 0.4V and error is still active then replace ECU. If voltage is lower then the harness is the root cause.', 'Trailer Control Module Pressure Sensor'),
(1339, 'xBS', 'C100022', 'Sensor signal voltage > 4.5V.', 'Signal Amplitude Greater Than Maximum', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and TCM. Disconnect connector on TCM side. Measure voltage between sensor signal and sensor signal ground. Voltage should be lower then 0.2V. If voltage is higher then there is a problem in the wiring harness. If voltage is lower then connect TCM and set the ECU to After market mode via diagnosis and measure again, if higher then 4.5V then replace TCM. If voltage is not higher then 4.5V, then measure on ECU side. If voltage there is lower then 4.5 V and error is still active then replace ECU.', 'Trailer Control Module Pressure Sensor'),
(1340, 'xBS', 'C100028', 'Sensor signal offset is out of range <0.5 or >0.85V.', 'Signal Bias Level Out of Range / Zero Adjustment Failure', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - Pneumatic problem - ECU damaged', 'Disconnect trailer. Set the ECU in After market mode via diagnosis. Release parking brake (SECURE VEHICLE). Disconnect connector on TCM side, measure voltage on the harness between sensor signal and sensor ground. If voltage is higher then 0.2V then repair wiring harness. If voltage is lower then connect TCM and measure pressure on yellow coupling head with all brakes released. If pressure is lower then (<0.1 bar) and the voltage on sensor signal is higher then 0.85V then replace TCM. If the pressure is higher then the 0.1 bar, then there is a pneumatic problem (TCM, parkbrake, FBM). Measure pressure on the parking brake input on the TCM (port 43), pressure should be higher than 6bar (KB to verify) all the time. If pressure is lower then check parking brake. Else check pressure on port 42 (backup) of TCM. If pressure is higher then 0.1 bar check footbrake module else replace TCM.', 'Trailer Control Module Pressure Sensor'),
(1341, 'xBS', 'C100112', 'Voltage > 5 V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check all cables and connectors from the TCM to the central ECU (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance of valve should be in [10..25] Ohm, resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm. If not ok then measure directly on TCM connector, alve should be in [10..25] Ohm. if not ok then replace TCM else repair wiring. Connect again on ECU side and disconnect from TCM side: Set ECU in AM mode: Measure voltage difference between valve and vehicle ground should be lower than 3 V. If not ok then repair harness. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate Inlet valve via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Trailer Control Module Inlet Valve'),
(1342, 'xBS', 'C100114', 'Voltage < 5 V', 'Circuit Short To Ground or Open', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check all cables and connectors from the TCM to the central ECU (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance of valve should be in [10..25] Ohm, resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector and to vehicle ground should be larger than 200 kOhm. If not ok then measure directly on TCM connector, valve should be in [10..25] Ohm. if not ok then replace TCM else repair wiring. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Trailer Control Module Inlet Valve'),
(1343, 'xBS', 'C100212', 'Voltage > 5 V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check all cables and connectors from the TCM to the central ECU (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance of valve should be in [10..25] Ohm, resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm. If not ok then measure directly on TCM connector, alve should be in [10..25] Ohm. if not ok then replace TCM else repair wiring. Connect again on ECU side and disconnect from TCM side: Set ECU in AM mode: Measure voltage difference between valve and vehicle ground should be lower than 3 V. If not ok then repair harness. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate Outlet valve via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Trailer Control Module Outlet Valve'),
(1344, 'xBS', 'C100214', 'Voltage < 5 V', 'Circuit Short To Ground or Open', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check all cables and connectors from the TCM to the central ECU (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance of valve should be in [10..25] Ohm, resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector and to vehicle ground should be larger than 200 kOhm. If not ok then measure directly on TCM connector, valve should be in [10..25] Ohm. if not ok then replace TCM else repair wiring. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Trailer Control Module Outlet Valve'),
(1345, 'xBS', 'C100312', 'Voltage > 5 V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check all cables and connectors from the TCM to the central ECU (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance of valve should be in [6..17] Ohm, resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm. If not ok then measure directly on TCM connector, alve should be in [6..17] Ohm. if not ok then replace TCM else repair wiring. Connect again on ECU side and disconnect from TCM side: Set ECU in AM mode: Measure voltage difference between valve and vehicle ground should be lower than 3 V. If not ok then repair harness. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate Backup valve via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Trailer Control Module Backup Valve'),
(1346, 'xBS', 'C100314', 'Voltage < 5 V', 'Circuit Short To Ground or Open', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check all cables and connectors from the TCM to the central ECU (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance of valve should be in [6..17] Ohm, resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector and to vehicle ground should be larger than 200 kOhm. If not ok then measure directly on TCM connector, valve should be in [6..17] Ohm. if not ok then replace TCM else repair wiring. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Trailer Control Module Backup Valve'),
(1347, 'xBS', 'C001011', 'Resistance between the output and the vehicle ground < 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
(1348, 'xBS', 'C001012', 'Voltage > 3 V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors to Inlet valve of PCV Left for short circuit to all other cables and pins (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm, voltage difference between valve and vehicle ground should be lower than 1 V. In case of lower resistance or higher voltage difference, repair wiring harness. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activat PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Left Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
(1349, 'xBS', 'C001013', 'Resistance at output > 1 kOhm..', 'Circuit Open', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If values are not ok replace PCV, otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
(1350, 'xBS', 'C00101A', 'Resistance between the output and the PCV ground < 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Resistance Below Threshold', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If values are not ok replace PCV, otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
(1351, 'xBS', 'C001095', 'Short circuit between inlet and outlet valve', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - ECU damaged', 'Check short circuit of all components where this type of fault is detected against each other. Disconnect central ECU and faulty PCV. Check short circuit of wire of PCV_FL_IV (highside of valve - X2/3) and wires of all other components where shorted channels were detected against each other. Insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm, otherwise repair faulty wires and/or connectors. If no fault found, reconnect the valves and repeat the previous measurement. If fault is still active, replace the PCV. If result is OK, reconnect everything, delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate the PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again, the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Left Front ABS Inlet Valve');
INSERT INTO `dtc_list` (`id`, `node`, `dtc_iso`, `failure_event`, `ftb_name`, `funct_behavior_desc`, `possible_root_cause`, `workshop_action`, `proprietary_name`) VALUES
(1352, 'xBS', 'C001111', 'Resistance between the output and the vehicle ground < 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1353, 'xBS', 'C001112', 'Voltage > 3 V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors to Inlet valve of PCV Left for short circuit to all other cables and pins (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm, voltage difference between valve and vehicle ground should be lower than 1 V. In case of lower resistance or higher voltage difference, repair wiring harness. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activat PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Left Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1354, 'xBS', 'C001113', 'Resistance at output > 1 kOhm.', 'Circuit Open', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If values are not ok replace PCV, otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1355, 'xBS', 'C00111A', 'Resistance between the output and the PCV ground < 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Resistance Below Threshold', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Left Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1356, 'xBS', 'C001163', 'Valve is set exhaust > 1 min (when using I/O DID PCV Valves, 0x1212).', 'Circuit / Component Protection Time-Out', NULL, 'Too long valve activation by Diag-I/O-control', 'Check if diagnostic command is shorter than 1 min.', 'Left Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1357, 'xBS', 'C001195', 'Short circuit between inlet and outlet valve', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - ECU damaged', 'Check short circuit of all components where this type of fault is detected against each other. Disconnect central ECU and faulty PCV. Check short circuit of wire of PCV_FL_IV (highside of valve - X2/3) and wires of all other components where shorted channels were detected against each other. Insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm, otherwise repair faulty wires and/or connectors. If no fault found, reconnect the valves and repeat the previous measurement. If fault is still active, replace the PCV. If result is OK, reconnect everything, delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate the PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again, the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Left Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1358, 'xBS', 'C001411', 'Resistance between the output and the vehicle ground < 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Right Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
