(1360, 'xBS', 'C001413', 'Resistance at output > 1 kOhm.', 'Circuit Open', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If values are not ok replace PCV, otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Right Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
(1361, 'xBS', 'C00141A', 'Resistance between the output and the PCV ground < 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Resistance Below Threshold', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV', 'Right Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
(1362, 'xBS', 'C001495', 'Short circuit between inlet and outlet valve', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - ECU damaged', 'Check short circuit of all components where this type of fault is detected against each other. Disconnect central ECU and faulty PCV. Check short circuit of wire of PCV_FL_IV (highside of valve - X2/3) and wires of all other components where shorted channels were detected against each other. Insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm, otherwise repair faulty wires and/or connectors. If no fault found, reconnect the valves and repeat the previous measurement. If fault is still active, replace the PCV. If result is OK, reconnect everything, delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate the PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again, the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Right Front ABS Inlet Valve'),
(1363, 'xBS', 'C001511', 'Resistance between the output and the vehicle ground < 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resitance between PCV and vehicle Gnd. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Right Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1364, 'xBS', 'C001512', 'Voltage > 3 V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors to Inlet valve of PCV Left for short circuit to all other cables and pins (including check for chafing damage). With valve wiring disconned from central ECU: resistance between actual valve connection and all wires of different components on the same connector should be larger than 200 kOhm, voltage difference between valve and vehicle ground should be lower than 1 V. In case of lower resistance or higher voltage difference, repair wiring harness. If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activat PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Right Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1365, 'xBS', 'C001513', 'Resistance at output > 1 kOhm.', 'Circuit Open', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If values are not ok replace PCV, otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Right Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1366, 'xBS', 'C00151A', 'Resistance between the output and the PCV ground < 5 Ohm.', 'Circuit Resistance Below Threshold', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - PCV damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling and connectors from ECU to PCV including chafing. Disconnect the wiring on the ECU side. 1) Measure resistance between Inlet/outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If result of measurement is not ok continue with 2) If result is ok reconnect everything delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again. The error is intermittent try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible. 2) Disconnect wiring from PCV Measure resistance between Inlet/Outlet Valve and PCV GND. Resistance must be between 10 and 22Ohm. If Values are not ok Replace PCV, Otherwise repair cabling harness.', 'Right Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1367, 'xBS', 'C001563', 'Valve is set exhaust > 1 min (when using I/O DID PCV Valves, 0x1212).', 'Circuit / Component Protection Time-Out', NULL, 'Too long valve activation by Diag-I/O-control', 'Check if diagnostic command is shorter than 1 min.', 'Right Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1368, 'xBS', 'C001595', 'Short circuit between inlet and outlet valve', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - ECU damaged', 'Check short circuit of all components where this type of fault is detected against each other. Disconnect central ECU and faulty PCV. Check short circuit of wire of PCV_FL_IV (highside of valve - X2/3) and wires of all other components where shorted channels were detected against each other. Insulation resistance must be higher than 200 kOhm, otherwise repair faulty wires and/or connectors. If no fault found, reconnect the valves and repeat the previous measurement. If fault is still active, replace the PCV. If result is OK, reconnect everything, delete error code, check if error code appears again (activate the PCV via diagnosis) . If error is not detected again, the error is intermittent, try to reproduce the error by moving cables and connectors. If error can not be reproduced no further action is possible.', 'Right Front ABS Outlet Valve'),
(1369, 'xBS', 'C109895', 'Short circuit between backup and inlet valve', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors (also for chafing damage) between central ECU and TCM; Disconnect connectors of the central ECU and of the TCM. Check for short circuit between the wires of the inlet and backup valves of the TCM. If resistance is lower than 200 kOhm, repair faults in the wiring; Measure resistance on the inlet and backup valve of the TCM directly on the TCM connector; If resistance is lower than 20 [Ohm], replace the TCM; Otherwise delete fault codes and try to move the harness to reproduce the fault.', 'Trailer Control Module Backup Valve And Inlet Valve'),
(1370, 'xBS', 'C109995', 'Short circuit between backup and outlet valve', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors (also for chafing damage) between central ECU and TCM; Disconnect connectors of the central ECU and of the TCM. Check for short circuit between the wires of the inlet and backup valves of the TCM. If resistance is lower than 200 kOhm, repair faults in the wiring; Measure resistance on the inlet and backup valve of the TCM directly on the TCM connector; If resistance is lower than 20 [Ohm], replace the TCM; Otherwise delete fault codes and try to move the harness to reproduce the fault.', 'Trailer Control Module Backup Valve And Outlet Valve'),
(1371, 'xBS', 'C109A95', 'Short circuit between inlet and outlet valve', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors (also for chafing damage) between central ECU and TCM; Disconnect connectors of the central ECU and of the TCM. Check for short circuit between the wires of the inlet and backup valves of the TCM. If resistance is lower than 200 kOhm, repair faults in the wiring; Measure resistance on the inlet and backup valve of the TCM directly on the TCM connector; If resistance is lower than 20 [Ohm], replace the TCM; Otherwise delete fault codes and try to move the harness to reproduce the fault.', 'Trailer Control Module Inlet Valve And Outlet Valve'),
(1372, 'xBS', 'C100712', 'Voltage > 5 V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and TCM (including check for chafing damage). Disconnect central ECU and TCM. Check the cables and connectors. Check cable and TCM resistances according to the values given in field detection. Connect the wiring to TCM: Check TCM voltages according to the values given in field detection; With wiring disconnected from both central ECU and TCM: resistance of each wire should be less than 3 [Ohm], resistance between any two wires and resistance between any wire and vehicle ground should be larger than 200 [kOhm]; With wiring disconnected from central ECU: resistance between TCM supply and inlet or outlet valve should be 12..23 [Ohm], resistance between TCM supply and backup valve should be 6..16 [Ohm]; In Aftermarket mode and with wiring disconnected from central ECU: voltage between any valve and TCM supply should be lower than 5 [V].', 'Trailer Control Modulator'),
(1373, 'xBS', 'C100714', 'Fault will be detected by activation of test pulse and reading back hardware status information.', 'Circuit Short To Ground or Open', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between central ECU and TCM (including check for chafing damage). Disconnect central ECU and TCM. Check the cables and connectors. Check cable and TCM resistances with wiring disconnected from central ECU: resistance between TCM supply and inlet or outlet valve should be [10 .. 25] Ohm, resistance between TCM supply and backup valve should be [6 .. 17] Ohm. If not ok measure the same thing on directly on the TCM. If not ok, replace TCM. If ok, then repair wiring harness. Resistance between any TCM pin and vehicle ground should be larger than 40 kOhm. If not ok on wire harness to the same test on TCM. If not ok on TCM, replace TCM else repair wiring harness.', 'Trailer Control Modulator'),
(1374, 'xBS', 'C10074A', 'TCM configured but not populated in ECU', 'Incorrect Component Installed', NULL, 'Wrong ECU hardware type', 'Check that ECU HW matches the chassi number. If not replace ECU.', 'Trailer Control Modulator'),
(1375, 'xBS', 'C100755', 'TCM detected, but not configured.', 'Not Configured', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Installed but not configured component', 'Check if configuration matches installation (check if TCM is installed and connected). If configuration matches installation, check connectors. If no fault is found with the connector, then check wiring (including check for chafing damage), and repair if faulty.', 'Trailer Control Modulator'),
(1376, 'xBS', 'C108829', 'Pressure sensor signal > 10 bar', 'Signal invalid', NULL, '- Supply pressure for TCM at supply pressure input is too high (APM) - Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - TCM damaged', 'Check maximum supply pressure for TCM at red coupling; Maximum supply pressure must be lower than 9,5 [bar]; If maximum supply pressure is correct; Measure pressure externally with 2 % precision on the yellow coupling head with brake pedal fully pressed; Compare the measured pressure with the TCM pressure read via diagnosis. In case of a difference higher than 0,5 [bar]+5 %; Check cables and connectors (to pressure sensor ground and signal) between ECU and TCM for damages, chafing marks, dirt, dust, water in the connectors; Replace the TCM', 'Trailer Control Module Pressure Control'),
(1377, 'xBS', 'C108864', 'Trailer brake is activated > 10 min', 'Signal Plausibility Failure', NULL, '- Damaged park brake(pressure output or signal from APM) - Damaged piping - Damaged/ too long usage of stretch brake - Damaged/ wrongly installed FBM (residual backup pressure without FBM actuation) - TCM damaged', 'Valve controlled trailer brake signal must have state deactivated, if valve controlled trailer brake is released. Check valve controlled trailer brake signal, and repair if faulty. Perform the needed reverse test procedure. If some other TCM related fault is reported during this procedure, follow the repair procedure of the reported fault.', 'Trailer Control Module Pressure Control'),
(1378, 'xBS', 'C108867', 'Implausible high pressure at end of braking and valve controlled trailer brake is activated implausibly long', 'Signal Incorrect After Event', NULL, '- TCM damaged - Valve controlled trailer brake signal is incorrect (it is always active)', 'Valve controlled trailer brake signal must have state deactivated, if valve controlled trailer brake is released. Check valve controlled trailer brake signal, and repair if faulty. Perform the needed reverse test procedure. If some other TCM related fault is reported during this procedure, follow the repair procedure of the reported fault.', 'Trailer Control Module Pressure Control'),
(1379, 'xBS', 'C108871', 'Backup pressure does not exceed minimum pressure level dependent on FBM stroke.', 'Actuator Stuck', NULL, '- Pneumatic pipes between FBM and TCM open or stuffed - Damage in the mechanical or pneumatic part of the FBM - Damaged parking brake(pressure output or signal from APM) - TCM damaged - Supply pressure at TCM supply pressure input is not sufficient, supply pressure circuit for trailer - Brake piping of the yellow coupling head open', 'Check backup piping between the FBM and the TCM, repair if faulty; Check the wiring and the connectors between the central ECU and the TCM, repair if faulty; Check piping between the supply pressure and the TCM, repair if faulty; Compare supply pressure of the TCM measured by external pressure gauge (with a maximum tolerance of 2%) with the supply pressure information transmitted by the APM. If the pressure difference is higher than 1 bar + 5%, then check the APM; Set ECU into Aftermarket Diagnostic Mode; Press the brake pedal fully; Check backup pressure increase from FBM with external pressure gauge with a maximum tolerance of 2%; Compare the backup pressure with the pressure of the TCM read via diagnosis; The dynamic behaviour of both signals must be similar. In case of a deviation, piping between the FBM and the TCM must be repaired; Otherwise the TCM is defect; Replace the TCM.', 'Trailer Control Module Pressure Control'),
(1380, 'xBS', 'C108872', 'Difference between pressure measured by TCM and demanded pressure > 1.5 bar', 'Actuator Stuck Open', NULL, '- TCM silencer plugged - TCM damaged - Damaged park brake(pressure output or signal from APM) - Damaged/ wrongly installed FBM (residual backup pressure without FBM actuation)', 'Disconnect trailer; Do the revers test to exclude temporary faults; Check parking brake valve by reading parking brake status from APM; Check the silencer of the TCM; Set ECU into Aftermarket Diagnostic Mode; Press the brake pedal fully and release it; Check pressure decrease with external pressure gauge with a maximum tolerance of 2%. Compare the measured pressure with the pressure of the TCM read via diagnosis; The dynamic behaviour of both signals must be similar; Check also for the correct release gradient; If not OK, replace the TCM; 1,5 [s] after brake pedal is released, pressure must be lower than 0,5 [bar]. If not OK, replace the TCM; Delete fault codes and check for the fault code; Check pressure on yellow coupling head with all brakes released (SECURE VEHICLE). Pressure on yellow coupling must be zero and the pressure read by diagnostics must also be zero; Measure on the parking brake input on the TCM (port 43), should be higher than 6 [bar] [KB to verify] all the time; Press brakepedal fully and release it fast, then the pressure on the yellow coupling must release fast (1 s); Activate parking brake and release it fast and the the pressure must release fast (1..1.5 s); After that the pressure on the PB input (port 43) has to be higher 6 [bar]; If the input pressure is not ok then the problem is between APM and TCM. Else, check parking brake and stretch brake signal. if no problem found on the signals, replace the TCM', 'Trailer Control Module Pressure Control'),
(1381, 'xBS', 'C108873', '- Difference between pressure measured by TCM and demanded pressure < 1.5 bar - Implausible inlet valve actuation ( if inlet valve protection is active, and actual pressure < 4bar and supply pressure of trailer circuit > 5bar.)', 'Actuator Stuck Closed', NULL, '- Damaged piping or part between TCM and trailer - Damaged piping or part between TCM and APM - TCM damaged - Damaged park brake(pressure output or signal from APM)', 'Disconnect trailer; Do the revers test to exclude temporary faults; Check pneumatic piping to the trailer including coupling head (high leakage); Check pneumatic piping to the APM (if piping is not according to the specification /i.e. wrong dimention, bend on the piping/, supply pressure information can be wrong); Compare supply pressure of the TCM measured by external pressure gauge (with a maximum tolerance of 2 %) with the supply pressure information transmitted by the APM; If the pressure difference is higher than 1 [bar] + 5 %, then check the APM; Check the wiring (pressure sensor ground and signal) between the TCM and the central ECU; Repair if faulty; Set ECU into Aftermarket Diagnostic Mode; Press the brake pedal fully; Check pressure of the TCM (yellow coupling) with an external pressure gauge with a maximum tolerance of 2 %; Compare the pressure with the pressure of the TCM read via diagnosis; If difference is higher than 0,5 [bar] + 5 % then replace the TCM; Otherwise delete fault codes and check for the fault code', 'Trailer Control Module Pressure Control'),
(1382, 'xBS', 'C200063', '- ABS activity is implausibly long - Too low brake pressures is required by ABS for an implausibly long time.', 'Circuit / Component Protection Time-Out', NULL, '- Fault of at least one wheel speed sensor or its mounting - Damages of at least one tone wheel, - Noisy wheel speed signal, - Differences in tyre sizes, - Puncture of a tyre, - Continuous brake force on a wheel (without brake pressure).', 'Check wheel speeds in snapshot to see, which wheel can cause the fault. Check tyre for size and correct air pressure, check pneumatic and mechanical parts of wheel brakes. Check wheel speed signal components: check cable, sensor and tone wheel. Check if pneumatic and electronic installation to wheels correspond to each other (if pneumatic pipes are mixed up). Check if configuration stored in the ECU corresponds to vehicle brake system layout: number and location of sensed wheels, axle type such as driven, liftable. Check if configuration stored in the central ECU corresponds to wheel rolling circumference and tone-wheel teeth number. If those do not conform, then correct the configuration values or change the part of the vehicle.', 'Anti-Lock Brake System'),
(1383, 'xBS', 'U114655', 'Ve hficle l ayolu t adn d configuration do not match.', 'Not Configured', NULL, 'Wrong dataset', 'Download vehicle layout matching dataset, if still active contact technical service', 'ESP Function Mode'),
(1384, 'xBS', 'C108D07', 'Difference between left and right pads of an axle > 20%', 'Mechanical Failures', NULL, '- Mechanical fault in the brake calipers - Damaged disc or brake pads. - Damaged Lining wear sensor', 'Measure actual wear values externally. Compare them with the wear values measured by the EBS system (read out via diagnostics). If they match, check brake calipers, disc and pads. calculate wear values, Check lining wear sensor Otherwise check connection resistance between lining wear sensor and EPM, including increased resitance of connectors due to e.g. corrosion.', 'Wheel 3 Braking Monitoring'),
(1385, 'xBS', 'C108D38', 'Frequent non symmetric axle internal slip is detected.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, '- Damaged brake or brake cylinder, - Dirtened moving brake parts such as brake pads/discs/drums (oil, grease) - Leaky piping between EPM and brake cylinder - Different tyre at axle (wear, tyre type, season type, aging) - Different brake pads/discs/drums at axle (wear, type, aging) - Vehicle one- side/asymmetric loaded for longer time - Damaged vehicle suspension - Incorrect adjusted track of vehicle - EPM damaged (different pressure left/right in case of 2CH EPM)', 'Measure actual wear values externally. Compare them with the wear values measured by the EBS system (read out via diagnostics). If they match, check brake calipers, disc and pads. calculate wear values, Check lining wear sensor Otherwise check connection resistance between lining wear sensor and EPM, including increased resitance of connectors due to e.g. corrosion.', 'Wheel 3 Braking Monitoring'),
(1386, 'xBS', 'C108D62', 'Current wheel speed differs (>25%) from the average of the other wheels.', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Tyre with wrong circumference is mounted - Puncture of the tyre - Continuous brake force on a wheel without brake activated by EBS. - Wrong tone wheel - Undetected fault of the wheel speed sensor', 'Check wheel brakes including actuator device and tyres according service instruction. Measure pressures in both brake chambers of the corresponding axle externally with 2% precision. Apply brake pedal until ca. 4 bar is reached. If difference between the two externally measured pressure is greater than 1 bar + 5% or pressure gradinets of the two sides are significally different then pneumatic piping between EPM and brake chamber should be checked. If there is no failure with the pneumatic piping, the EPM should be checked as follows: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics increased from 0 to 8 bar with 1 bar steps. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. In case of changed components run diagnostic routine reinitializeSelfLearnedParameters.', 'Wheel 3 Braking Monitoring'),
(1387, 'xBS', 'C108C07', 'Difference between left and right pads of an axle > 20%', 'Mechanical Failures', NULL, '- Mechanical fault in the brake calipers - Damaged disc or brake pads. - Damaged Lining wear sensor', 'Measure actual wear values externally. Compare them with the wear values measured by the EBS system (read out via diagnostics). If they match, check brake calipers, disc and pads. calculate wear values, Check lining wear sensor Otherwise check connection resistance between lining wear sensor and EPM, including increased resitance of connectors due to e.g. corrosion.', 'Wheel 2 Braking Monitoring'),
(1388, 'xBS', 'C108C38', 'Frequent non symmetric axle internal slip is detected.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, '- Damaged brake or brake cylinder, - Dirtened moving brake parts such as brake pads/discs/drums (oil, grease) - Leaky piping between EPM and brake cylinder - Different tyre at axle (wear, tyre type, season type, aging) - Different brake pads/discs/drums at axle (wear, type, aging) - Vehicle one- side/asymmetric loaded for longer time - Damaged vehicle suspension - Incorrect adjusted track of vehicle - EPM damaged (different pressure left/right in case of 2CH EPM)', 'Check wheel brakes including actuator device and tyres according service instruction. Measure pressures in both brake chambers of the corresponding axle externally with 2% precision. Apply brake pedal until ca. 4 bar is reached. If difference between the two externally measured pressure is greater than 1 bar + 5% or pressure gradinets of the two sides are significally different then pneumatic piping between EPM and brake chamber should be checked. If there is no failure with the pneumatic piping, the EPM should be checked as follows: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics increased from 0 to 8 bar with 1 bar steps. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. In case of changed components run diagnostic routine reinitializeSelfLearnedParameters.', 'Wheel 2 Braking Monitoring'),
(1389, 'xBS', 'C108C62', 'Current wheel speed differs (>25%) from the average of the other wheels.', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '- Tyre with wrong circumference is mounted - Puncture of the tyre - Continuous brake force on a wheel without brake activated by EBS. - Wrong tone wheel - Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Undetected fault of the wheel speed sensor', 'Check tire and check the brakes. If error still active, check Wheel speed sensors by driving and monitoring. Wheel speed shall not differ more than 25 %. check tone wheel', 'Wheel 2 Braking Monitoring'),
(1390, 'xBS', 'C108707', 'Difference between left and right pads of an axle > 20%', 'Mechanical Failures', NULL, '- Mechanical fault in the brake calipers - Damaged disc or brake pads. - Damaged Lining wear sensor', 'Measure actual wear values externally. Compare them with the wear values measured by the EBS system (read out via diagnostics). If they match, check brake calipers, disc and pads. calculate wear values, Check lining wear sensor Otherwise check connection resistance between lining wear sensor and EPM, including increased resitance of connectors due to e.g. corrosion.', 'Wheel 1 Braking Monitoring'),
(1391, 'xBS', 'C108738', 'Frequent non symmetric axle internal slip is detected.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, '- Damaged brake or brake cylinder, - Dirtened moving brake parts such as brake pads/discs/drums (oil, grease) - Leaky piping between EPM and brake cylinder - Different tyre at axle (wear, tyre type, season type, aging) - Different brake pads/discs/drums at axle (wear, type, aging) - Vehicle one- side/asymmetric loaded for longer time - Damaged vehicle suspension - Incorrect adjusted track of vehicle - EPM damaged (different pressure left/right in case of 2CH EPM)vehicle one- side/asymmetric loaded for longer time, damaged vehicle suspension,', 'Check wheel brakes including actuator device and tyres according service instruction. Measure pressures in both brake chambers of the corresponding axle externally with 2% precision. Apply brake pedal until ca. 4 bar is reached. If difference between the two externally measured pressure is greater than 1 bar + 5% or pressure gradinets of the two sides are significally different then pneumatic piping between EPM and brake chamber should be checked. If there is no failure with the pneumatic piping, the EPM should be checked as follows: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics increased from 0 to 8 bar with 1 bar steps. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. In case of changed components run diagnostic routine reinitializeSelfLearnedParameters.', 'Wheel 1 Braking Monitoring'),
(1392, 'xBS', 'C108762', 'Current wheel speed differs (>25%) from the average of the other wheels.', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '- Tyre wit h dwrongd k f circumference is mounted - Puncture of the tyre - Continuous brake force on a wheel without brake activated by EBS. - Wrong tone wheel - Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Undetected fault of the wheel speed sensor', 'Check tire and check the brakes. If error still active, check Wheel speed sensors by driving and monitoring. Wheel speed shall not differ more than 25 %. check tone wheel', 'Wheel 1 Braking Monitoring'),
(1393, 'xBS', 'C108E07', 'Difference between left and right pads of an axle > 20%', 'Mechanical Failures', NULL, '- Mechanical fault in the brake calipers - Damaged disc or brake pads. - Damaged Lining wear sensor', 'Measure actual wear values externally. Compare them with the wear values measured by the EBS system (read out via diagnostics). If they match, check brake calipers, disc and pads. calculate wear values, Check lining wear sensor Otherwise check connection resistance between lining wear sensor and EPM, including increased resitance of connectors due to e.g. corrosion.', 'Wheel 4 Braking Monitoring'),
(1394, 'xBS', 'C108E38', 'Frequent non symmetric axle internal slip is detected.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, '- Damaged brake or brake cylinder, - Dirtened moving brake parts such as brake pads/discs/drums (oil, grease) - Leaky piping between EPM and brake cylinder - Different tyre at axle (wear, tyre type, season type, aging) - Different brake pads/discs/drums at axle (wear, type, aging) - Vehicle one- side/asymmetric loaded for longer time - Damaged vehicle suspension - Incorrect adjusted track of vehicle - EPM damaged (different pressure left/right in case of 2CH EPM)', 'Check wheel brakes including actuator device and tyres according service instruction. Measure pressures in both brake chambers of the corresponding axle externally with 2% precision. Apply brake pedal until ca. 4 bar is reached. If difference between the two externally measured pressure is greater than 1 bar + 5% or pressure gradinets of the two sides are significally different then pneumatic piping between EPM and brake chamber should be checked. If there is no failure with the pneumatic piping, the EPM should be checked as follows: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics increased from 0 to 8 bar with 1 bar steps. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. In case of changed components run diagnostic routine reinitializeSelfLearnedParameters.', 'Wheel 4 Braking Monitoring'),
(1395, 'xBS', 'C108E62', 'Current wheel speed differs (>25%) from the average of the other wheels.', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '- Tyre with wrong circumference is mounted - Puncture of the tyre - Continuous brake force on a wheel without brake activated by EBS. - Wrong tone wheel - Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Undetected fault of the wheel speed sensorr)', 'Check tire and check the brakes. If error still active, check Wheel speed sensors by driving and monitoring. Wheel speed shall not differ more than 25 %. check tone wheel', 'Wheel 4 Braking Monitoring'),
(1396, 'xBS', 'C108F07', 'Difference between left and right pads of an axle > 20%', 'Mechanical Failures', NULL, '- Mechanical fault in the brake calipers - Damaged disc or brake pads. - Damaged Lining wear sensor', 'Measure actual wear values externally. Compare them with the wear values measured by the EBS system (read out via diagnostics). If they match, check brake calipers, disc and pads. calculate wear values, Check lining wear sensor Otherwise check connection resistance between lining wear sensor and EPM, including increased resitance of connectors due to e.g. corrosion.', 'Wheel 5 Braking Monitoring'),
(1397, 'xBS', 'C108F38', 'Frequent non symmetric axle internal slip is detected.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, '- Damaged brake or brake cylinder, - Dirtened moving brake parts such as brake pads/discs/drums (oil, grease) - Leaky piping between EPM and brake cylinder - Different tyre at axle (wear, tyre type, season type, aging) - Different brake pads/discs/drums at axle (wear, type, aging) - Vehicle one- side/asymmetric loaded for longer time - Damaged vehicle suspension - Incorrect adjusted track of vehicle - EPM damaged (different pressure left/right in case of 2CH EPM)er time, damaged vehicle suspension, incorrect adjusted track of vehicle, damaged EPM', 'Check wheel brakes including actuator device and tyres according service instruction. Measure pressures in both brake chambers of the corresponding axle externally with 2% precision. Apply brake pedal until ca. 4 bar is reached. If difference between the two externally measured pressure is greater than 1 bar + 5% or pressure gradinets of the two sides are significally different then pneumatic piping between EPM and brake chamber should be checked. If there is no failure with the pneumatic piping, the EPM should be checked as follows: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics increased from 0 to 8 bar with 1 bar steps. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. In case of changed components run diagnostic routine reinitializeSelfLearnedParameters.', 'Wheel 5 Braking Monitoring'),
(1398, 'xBS', 'C108F62', 'Current wheel speed differs (>25%) from the average of the other wheels.', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '(-d Tyffre with wrong lf/ h circumference is mounted - Puncture of the tyre - Continuous brake force on a wheel without brake activated by EBS. - Wrong tone wheel - Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Undetected fault of the wheel speed sensor', 'Check tire and check the brakes. If error still active, check Wheel speed sensors by driving and monitoring. Wheel speed shall not differ more than 25 %. check tone wheel', 'Wheel 5 Braking Monitoring'),
(1399, 'xBS', 'C109007', 'Difference between left and right pads of an axle > 20%', 'Mechanical Failures', NULL, '- Mechanical fault in the brake calipers - Damaged disc or brake pads. - Damaged Lining wear sensor', 'Measure actual wear values externally. Compare them with the wear values measured by the EBS system (read out via diagnostics). If they match, check brake calipers, disc and pads. calculate wear values, Check lining wear sensor Otherwise check connection resistance between lining wear sensor and EPM, including increased resitance of connectors due to e.g. corrosion.', 'Wheel 6 Braking Monitoring'),
(1400, 'xBS', 'C109038', 'Frequent non symmetric axle internal slip is detected.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, '- Damaged brake or brake cylinder, - Dirtened moving brake parts such as brake pads/discs/drums (oil, grease) - Leaky piping between EPM and brake cylinder - Different tyre at axle (wear, tyre type, season type, aging) - Different brake pads/discs/drums at axle (wear, type, aging) - Vehicle one- side/asymmetric loaded for longer time - Damaged vehicle suspension - Incorrect adjusted track of vehicle - EPM damaged (different pressure left/right in case of 2CH EPM)', 'Check wheel brakes including actuator device and tyres according service instruction. Measure pressures in both brake chambers of the corresponding axle externally with 2% precision. Apply brake pedal until ca. 4 bar is reached. If difference between the two externally measured pressure is greater than 1 bar + 5% or pressure gradinets of the two sides are significally different then pneumatic piping between EPM and brake chamber should be checked. If there is no failure with the pneumatic piping, the EPM should be checked as follows: Ensure that reservoirs are fully charged (until cut-off pressure). Switch to Aftermarket mode with diagnostics. Control pressure at EPM via diagnostics increased from 0 to 8 bar with 1 bar steps. Read pressure values via diagnostics. Measure pressure in brake chamber externally with 2% precision. If difference between read and externally measured pressure is greater than 0.5 bar + 5%, then EPM should be replaced. In case of changed components run diagnostic routine reinitializeSelfLearnedParameters.', 'Wheel 6 Braking Monitoring'),
(1401, 'xBS', 'C109062', 'Current wheel speed differs (>25%) from the average of the other wheels.', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '- Tyre with wrong circumference is mounted - Puncture of the tyre - Continuous brake force on a wheel without brake activated by EBS. - Wrong tone wheel - Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Undetected fault of the wheel speed sensor', 'Check tire and check the brakes. If error still active, check Wheel speed sensors by driving and monitoring. Wheel speed shall not differ more than 25 %. check tone wheel', 'Wheel 6 Braking Monitoring'),
(1402, 'xBS', 'C109107', 'Difference between left and right pads of an axle > 20%', 'Mechanical Failures', NULL, '- Mechanical fault in the brake calipers - Damaged disc or brake pads. - Damaged Lining wear sensor', 'Measure actual wear values externally. Compare them with the wear values measured by the EBS system (read out via diagnostics). If they match, check brake calipers, disc and pads. calculate wear values, Check lining wear sensor Otherwise check connection resistance between lining wear sensor and EPM, including increased resitance of connectors due to e.g. corrosion.', 'Wheel 7 Braking Monitoring'),
