(1413, 'xBS', 'C109462', 'Current wheel speed differs (>25%) from the average of the other wheels.', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '- Tyre with wrong circumference is mounted - Puncture of the tyre - Continuous brake force on a wheel without brake activated by EBS. - Wrong tone wheel - Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Undetected fault of the wheel speed sensor', 'Check tire and check the brakes. If error still active, check Wheel speed sensors by driving and monitoring. Wheel speed shall not differ more than 25 %. check tone wheel', 'Wheel 10 Braking Monitoring'),
(1414, 'xBS', 'C109695', 'Wheel speeds on one axle during curve driving is not plausible.', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) (Right and left hand side sensors are switched)', 'Check the installation order of the wheel speed sensors of the affected axle; If installation is correct check dataset for correct configuration', 'Wheel Speed Sensor Configuration'),
(1415, 'xBS', 'U115E55', 'Configuration is not correct for the inteligent slip control', 'Not Configured', NULL, 'False parameters for ISC in configuration', 'Download correct dataset, if still active contect technical service', 'Intelligent Slip Control Configuration'),
(1416, 'xBS', 'U116107', 'Difference between demanded deceleration and actual deceleration is too high.', 'Mechanical Failures', NULL, '- Not sufficient supply pressure - Fading or damaged brakes - overload', 'Check for overloaded vehicle/trailer.', 'Vehicle Braking State'),
(1417, 'xBS', 'U116168', 'Calculated disc temperature > 550 degrees', 'Event Information', NULL, '- The brakes were overstressed (too frequent and long activation no time for cooling). - Wrong Ambient temperature or time/date information - Vehicle construction changed in a way that estimation parameters are no longer valid', 'Driver should use a less agressive driving style, check tires for right size (cooling condition), download correct dataset', 'Vehicle Braking State'),
(1418, 'xBS', 'U116177', 'Vehicle deceleration does not match to the demaned deceleration within a tolerance in normal vehicle condition.', 'Commanded Position Not Reachable', NULL, '- Software error - ECU damage', 'Check for sufficient supply pressure, check for fading brakes, overloaded vehicle/trailer, check the piping and the brakes, if fault becomes still active and the whole mechanical brake system is ok. for info: Wrong vehicle weight do not cause this error', 'Vehicle Braking State'),
(1419, 'xBS', 'C107211', 'FBM supply soft short to ground', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - ECU damaged', 'Check cabling => acceptable minimum voltage on the power supply line (FBM_SPL) from ECU to DFBM min: 10 [V] (during ignition is on and off); If the problem still persists replace the central ECU; If the problem still persists replace the FBM', 'Foot Brake Module Electrical Link'),
(1420, 'xBS', 'C107212', '- Communication from the ECU to the dFBM (S2) is disturbed. - Power down process of FBM does not work - FBM send continuous status message to the ECU because of missing task trigger. is working properly.', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - FBM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the wiring and connectors between the central ECU and the foot brake module (especially S2 signal) Measure insulation resitance of foot brake module wires to vehicle GND and all X1 of central ECU wires against S2 signal with disconnected Central ECU and disconnected FBM. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm If resitance is lower repair wiring. Mesure resitance of foot brake module wires between foot brake module and Central ECU (especially S2 signal). Resistance must be lower than 5Ohm If resistance is higher repair wiring. If wiring is ok and error is still avtive measure signal voltage on S2 line. If oltage is lower than 1,5V replace foot brake moduleM otherwise replace Central ECU', 'Foot Brake Module Electrical Link'),
(1421, 'xBS', 'C107282', 'FBM message counter is inconsistent with timestamp of reception', 'Alive / Sequence Counter Incorrect / Not Updated', NULL, 'FBM damaged', 'Replace foot brake module.', 'Foot Brake Module Electrical Link'),
(1422, 'xBS', 'C107287', 'Pedal position data missing or no valid data is received from FBM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - FBM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the wiring and connectors between the central ECU and the foot brake module Measure insulation resistance of all foot brake module wires to vehicle ground and to all other wires on the ECU-X1 connector with disconnected Central ECU and disconnected FBM. Resistance must be higher than 200kOhm If resitance is lower repair wiring Mesure resitance of all foot brake module wires between foot brake module and central ECU. Resistance must be lower than 5Ohm If resistance is higher repair wiring. If error is still active and no error found measure signal S1 with scope. If signal is toggling between 0,5 and 4,5V replace ECU otherwise replace foot brake module or measure voltage on S1 line with voltage meter. If voltage is between 1.5 and 3.5V replace ECU otherwise replace foot brake module.', 'Foot Brake Module Electrical Link'),
(1423, 'xBS', 'C107294', '- The stroke sensed by the two stroke sensors is not identical, but the offset is still within a tolerable range - The wakeup switch position does not match the measured stroke value', 'Unexpected Operation', NULL, '- Rod is not according to the specification - FBM damaged', 'Check rod from pedal for foot brake module activation for correct part If rod is according to the specification replace the foot brake module.', 'Foot Brake Module Electrical Link'),
(1424, 'xBS', 'C107128', 'Too high offset internaly in FBM.', 'Signal Bias Level Out of Range / Zero Adjustment Failure', NULL, '- FBM is blocked (stuck in actuated position) - Incorrect mounting/installation - FBM damaged', 'Check if rod for activation of foot brake module has enough clearence (installtion manual). Adjust if needed. Do revers test and if the error do not disapear replace foot brake module.', 'Foot Brake Module'),
(1425, 'xBS', 'C107141', 'Checksum error of the drive software is detected in the A or B controller by the bootloader of the DFBM', 'General Checksum Failure', NULL, 'FBM damaged', 'Download again the digitial foot brake module software, if the fault is still active Replace foot brake module', 'Foot Brake Module'),
(1426, 'xBS', 'C107142', 'Flash, EEPROM or RAM memory fault', 'General Memory Failure', NULL, 'FBM damaged', 'Replace foot brake module', 'Foot Brake Module'),
(1427, 'xBS', 'C107149', 'Internal fault in the foot brake module', 'Internal Electronic Failure', NULL, 'FBM damaged', 'Download latest software version to the foot brake module, if fault is still active, Replace foot brake Module.', 'Foot Brake Module'),
(1428, 'xBS', 'C10714A', '- Invalid FBM hardware type - Incompatibility is detected by the central ECU between the FBM and the central ECU', 'Incorrect Component Installed', NULL, 'Wrong FBM hardware is mounted', '- Check part number on foot brake module, replace foot brake module with correct part number - Check that the MSW is the latest SW. If not, download new Central ECU SW.', 'Foot Brake Module'),
(1429, 'xBS', 'C10714B', 'One of the two dFBM temperature sensors delivers an implausible value.', 'Over Temperature', NULL, 'FBM damaged', 'Replace the foot brake module', 'Foot Brake Module'),
(1430, 'xBS', 'C107194', 'Incompatible SW parts in dFBM', 'Unexpected Operation', NULL, 'FBM damaged', 'Update the foot brake module with compatible boot/driver SW for the used hardware, if the fault is still active check Replace foot brake module.', 'Foot Brake Module'),
(1431, 'xBS', 'C107195', 'Wakeup time of the system when ignition is off > 1h', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, '- FBM is blocked (stuck in actuated position) - Incorrect mounting/installation - FBM damaged', 'Check if rod for activation of foot brake module has enough clearence (installtion manual). Adjust if needed, if adjustment not successful then replace foot brake module.', 'Foot Brake Module'),
(1432, 'xBS', 'U116368', 'CRC or messsage counter error in external brake demand messages', 'Event Information', NULL, 'Damaged sending ECU', 'Failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting BBM, DACU or TECU signals.', 'External Brake Request Message Checksum'),
(1433, 'xBS', 'C109768', 'Roller test bench mode activated.', 'Event Information', NULL, 'Roller test bench mode was activated by diagnostic routine or instrument cluster activatation.', 'No action required, it is not a failure, only an event information (Roller Test Bench Mode is active)', 'Roller Test Bench Mode'),
(1434, 'xBS', 'C10894A', 'Rear axle steering circuits is not populated in ECU but configured.', 'Incorrect Component Installed', NULL, 'Wrong ECU type', 'Check if configuration matches installation. Download correct dataset.', 'Rear Active Steering Control Valves'),
(1435, 'xBS', 'C108955', 'Valves or rear angle sensor is detected, but not configured.', 'Not Configured', NULL, 'Installed but not configured components.', 'Check if configuration matches installation. Download correct dataset.', 'Rear Active Steering Control Valves'),
(1436, 'xBS', 'C109C62', 'Sensor signal is implausible compared to wheel speeds signals', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '- Sensor is incorrectly calibrated - Drive of the sensor defect - Incorrect mounting - Steering system does not correspond to the vehicle specification (wrong steering gearbox or steering gear arm) - Sensor damaged - Wheelbase or wheeltrack do not correspond to the vehicle specification - Calibrated vehicle speed (C3) does not correspond to the wheel speeds', '- Check steering wheel angle sensor calibration - Check steering wheel angle sensor installation - Check Steering system (Steering gear etc.)', 'Rear Active Steering Internal Signal'),
(1437, 'xBS', 'C109C68', 'Internal EBS signals not available i.e. steering wheel angle or wheel speed is not available.', 'Event Information', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sensor', 'See other steering angle sensor or wheel speed sensor related faults', 'Rear Active Steering Internal Signal'),
(1438, 'xBS', 'C101721', 'Sensor signal < 0.25 V', 'Signal Amplitude Less Than Minimum', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and Lining wear sensor. Switch on lining wear sensor supply with diagnostics and read recorded voltage values (readLiningWearSensorValues_Start, readLiningWearSensorValues_Stop, readLiningWearSensorValues_Results). Perform voltage measurement externally (between LWS GND and LWS signal) during the time period, when lining wear sensor supply is switch on. If measured value is not within range 0.25-4,75V (EOL values) the problem is in the sensor or wiring. Compare values recorded by diagnostics and measured externally. If the values do not match (within 10% tolerance), EPM should be changed. If the values match disconnect lining wear sensor connector from EPM. Measure resistance of sensor to - vehicle ground, it should be larger than 200kOhm. - Then with wiring disconnected from both EPM and lining wear sensor: Resistance of each wire should be less than 5 Ohm and resistance between two pins of the wiring should be larger than 200 kOhm If all values are correct then wiring is OK, and sensor should be replaced. (- lining wear sensor supply, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for possible measurements (- lining wear sensor ground, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for possible measurements', 'Lining Wear Sensor 1'),
(1439, 'xBS', 'C101722', 'Sensor signal > 4.75 V', 'Signal Amplitude Greater Than Maximum', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and Lining wear sensor. Switch on lining wear sensor supply with diagnostics and read recorded voltage values (readLiningWearSensorValues_Start, readLiningWearSensorValues_Stop, readLiningWearSensorValues_Results). Perform voltage measurement externally (between LWS GND and LWS signal) during the time period, when lining wear sensor supply is switch on. If measured value is not within range 0.25-4,75V (EOL values) the problem is in the sensor or wiring. Compare values recorded by diagnostics and measured externally. If the values do not match (within 10% tolerance), EPM should be changed. If the values match disconnect lining wear sensor connector from EPM. Measure resistance of sensor to - vehicle ground, it should be larger than 200kOhm. - Then with wiring disconnected from both EPM and lining wear sensor: Resistance of each wire should be less than 5 Ohm and resistance between two pins of the wiring should be larger than 200 kOhm If all values are correct then wiring is OK, and sensor should be replaced. (- lining wear sensor supply, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for possible measurements (- lining wear sensor ground, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for', 'Lining Wear Sensor 1'),
(1440, 'xBS', 'C101821', 'Sensor signal < 0.25 V', 'Signal Amplitude Less Than Minimum', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Checkb lth e cables and connectors between EPM and Lining wear sensor. Switch on lining wear sensor supply with diagnostics and read recorded voltage values (readLiningWearSensorValues_Start, readLiningWearSensorValues_Stop, readLiningWearSensorValues_Results). Perform voltage measurement externally (between LWS GND and LWS signal) during the time period, when lining wear sensor supply is switch on. If measured value is not within range 0.25-4,75V (EOL values) the problem is in the sensor or wiring. Compare values recorded by diagnostics and measured externally. If the values do not match (within 10% tolerance), EPM should be changed. If the values match disconnect lining wear sensor connector from EPM. Measure resistance of sensor to - vehicle ground, it should be larger than 200kOhm. - Then with wiring disconnected from both EPM and lining wear sensor: Resistance of each wire should be less than 5 Ohm and resistance between two pins of the wiring should be larger than 200 kOhm If all values are correct then wiring is OK, and sensor should be replaced. (- lining wear sensor supply, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for possible measurements (- lining wear sensor ground, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for possible measurements', 'Lining Wear Sensor 2'),
(1441, 'xBS', 'C101822', 'Sensor signal > 4.75 V', 'Signal Amplitude Greater Than Maximum', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and Lining wear sensor. Switch on lining wear sensor supply with diagnostics and read recorded voltage values (readLiningWearSensorValues_Start, readLiningWearSensorValues_Stop, readLiningWearSensorValues_Results). Perform voltage measurement externally (between LWS GND and LWS signal) during the time period, when lining wear sensor supply is switch on. If measured value is not within range 0.25-4,75V (EOL values) the problem is in the sensor or wiring. Compare values recorded by diagnostics and measured externally. If the values do not match (within 10% tolerance), EPM should be changed. If the values match disconnect lining wear sensor connector from EPM. Measure resistance of sensor to - vehicle ground, it should be larger than 200kOhm. - Then with wiring disconnected from both EPM and lining wear sensor: Resistance of each wire should be less than 5 Ohm and resistance between two pins of the wiring should be larger than 200 kOhm If all values are correct then wiring is OK, and sensor should be replaced. (- lining wear sensor supply, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for possible measurements (- lining wear sensor ground, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for possible measurements', 'Lining Wear Sensor 2'),
(1442, 'xBS', 'C101921', 'Sensor signal < 0.25 V', 'Signal Amplitude Less Than Minimum', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and Lining wear sensor. Switch on lining wear sensor supply with diagnostics and read recorded voltage values (readLiningWearSensorValues_Start, readLiningWearSensorValues_Stop, readLiningWearSensorValues_Results). Perform voltage measurement externally (between LWS GND and LWS signal) during the time period, when lining wear sensor supply is switch on. If measured value is not within range 0.25-4,75V (EOL values) the problem is in the sensor or wiring. Compare values recorded by diagnostics and measured externally. If the values do not match (within 10% tolerance), EPM should be changed. If the values match disconnect lining wear sensor connector from EPM. Measure resistance of sensor to - vehicle ground, it should be larger than 200kOhm. - Then with wiring disconnected from both EPM and lining wear sensor: Resistance of each wire should be less than 5 Ohm and resistance between two pins of the wiring should be larger than 200 kOhm If all values are correct then wiring is OK, and sensor should be replaced. (- lining wear sensor supply, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for possible measurements', 'Lining Wear Sensor 3'),
(1443, 'xBS', 'C101922', 'Sensor signal > 4.75 V', 'Signal Amplitude Greater Than Maximum', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and Lining wear sensor. Switch on lining wear sensor supply with diagnostics and read recorded voltage values (readLiningWearSensorValues_Start, readLiningWearSensorValues_Stop, readLiningWearSensorValues_Results). Perform voltage measurement externally (between LWS GND and LWS signal) during the time period, when lining wear sensor supply is switch on. If measured value is not within range 0.25-4,75V (EOL values) the problem is in the sensor or wiring. Compare values recorded by diagnostics and measured externally. If the values do not match (within 10% tolerance), EPM should be changed. If the values match disconnect lining wear sensor connector from EPM. Measure resistance of sensor to - vehicle ground, it should be larger than 200kOhm. - Then with wiring disconnected from both EPM and lining wear sensor: Resistance of each wire should be less than 5 Ohm and resistance between two pins of the wiring should be larger than 200 kOhm If all values are correct then wiring is OK, and sensor should be replaced. (- lining wear sensor supply, it should be in range of [to be defined by V3P] Ohm) V3P to check for possible', 'Lining Wear Sensor 3'),
