(1477, 'xBS', 'C104855', 'ALS is configured but no signal or sensor supply detected.', 'Not Configured', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from the ALS to the corresponding EPM (including check for chafing damage). If no error found, check the EoL parameters. If no error found, check with other ALS. If error still active, check with other EPM (check that the EPM is prepared for ALS connected) . If error still active, check with other central ECU.', 'Wheel 10 Axle Load Sensor'),
(1478, 'xBS', 'C104911', 'Supply voltage < 4.5V', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors of all LWS that are connected to the EPM that supplies the LWS, which is indicated by DTC (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. Disconnect first the lining wear sensor from EPM where the DTC points on. Switch on lining wear sensor supply with diagnostics and read recorded supply voltage values (readLiningWearSensorValues_Start, readLiningWearSensorValues_Stop, readLiningWearSensorValues_Results). Perform voltage measurement of lining wear sensor output of EPM externally during the time period, when lining wear sensor supply is switch on. Compare values recorded by diagnostics and measured externally. Lining wear supply will not remain on as long as a defective Sensor connected to the corresponding EPM. In this case reconnect tested sensor, disconnect the next one and repeat process. Repeat until all Sensors of corresponding EPM have been disconnected once and readLiningWearSensorValues_Results delivers a plausible result (see below). If the values do not match (tolerance 10%), or they are out of range (4.5V...5.5V), EPM should be changed. With wiring disconnected from both EPM and lining wear sensor: resistance of each wire should be less than 3 Ohm, and resistance between two pins of the wiring should be larger than 200 kOhm. If all values are correct then wiring is OK, and sensor should be replaced', 'Wheel 1 Brake Lining Wear Supply Circuit'),
(1479, 'xBS', 'C104912', 'Supply voltage > 6V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from all LWS that are connected to the EPM that supplies the LWS, which is indicated by DTC (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. Disconnect first the lining wear sensor from EPM where the DTC points on. Measure the lining wear sensor supply externally with lining wear sensor supply deactivated. The voltage must be below 0.5V. Repeat for each LWS that is connected to the corresponding EPM. If not replace EPM. Activate the lining wear supply and the value shall be within 4.5-5.5V. If not replace EPM. Disconnect also EPM from central ECU. Check resistance between voltage supply pin of wire to EPM and wire to lining wear sensor supply. If resistance is smaller than 200 kOhm then error is in the wiring.', 'Wheel 1 Brake Lining Wear Supply Circuit'),
(1480, 'xBS', 'C104924', 'Sensor signal > 0.5V', 'Signal Stuck High', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from all LWS that are connected to the EPM that supplies the LWS which is indicated by DTC (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. Disconnect first the lining wear sensor from EPM where the DTC points on. Measure the lining wear sensor supply externally with lining wear sensor supply deactivated and the voltage must be below 0.5V. Repeat for each LWS that is connected to the corresponding EPM. If not replace EPM. Activate the lining wear supply and the value shall be within 4.5-5.5V. If not replace EPM. Disconnect also EPM from central ECU. Check resistance between voltage supply pin of wire to EPM and wire to lining wear sensor supply. If resistance is smaller than 200 kOhm then error is in the wiring.', 'Wheel 1 Brake Lining Wear Supply Circuit'),
