(1503, 'xBS', 'C105112', 'Supply voltage > 6V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from all LWS that are connected to the EPM that supplies the LWS, which is indicated by DTC (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. Disconnect first the lining wear sensor from EPM where the DTC points on. Measure the lining wear sensor supply externally with lining wear sensor supply deactivated. The voltage must be below 0.5V. Repeat for each LWS that is connected to the corresponding EPM. If not replace EPM. Activate the lining wear supply and the value shall be within 4.5-5.5V. If not replace EPM. Disconnect also EPM from central ECU. Check resistance between voltage supply pin of wire to EPM and wire to lining wear sensor supply. If resistance is smaller than 200 kOhm then error is in the wiring.', 'Wheel 9 Brake Lining Wear Supply Circuit'),
