(1505, 'xBS', 'C105211', 'Supply voltage < 4.5V', 'Circuit Short To Ground', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors of all LWS that are connected to the EPM that supplies the LWS, which is indicated by DTC (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. Disconnect first the lining wear sensor from EPM where the DTC points on. Switch on lining wear sensor supply with diagnostics and read recorded supply voltage values (readLiningWearSensorValues_Start, readLiningWearSensorValues_Stop, readLiningWearSensorValues_Results). Perform voltage measurement of lining wear sensor output of EPM externally during the time period, when lining wear sensor supply is switch on. Compare values recorded by diagnostics and measured externally. Lining wear supply will not remain on as long as a defective Sensor connected to the corresponding EPM. In this case reconnect tested sensor, disconnect the next one and repeat process. Repeat until all Sensors of corresponding EPM have been disconnected once and readLiningWearSensorValues_Results delivers a plausible result (see below). If the values do not match (tolerance 10%), or they are out of range (4.5V...5.5V), EPM should be changed. With wiring disconnected from both EPM and lining wear sensor: resistance of each wire should be less than 3 Ohm, and resistance between two pins of the wiring should be larger than 200 kOhm. If all values are correct then wiring is OK, and sensor should be replaced', 'Wheel 10 Brake Lining Wear Supply Circuit'),
(1506, 'xBS', 'C105212', 'Supply voltage > 6V', 'Circuit Short To Battery', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from all LWS that are connected to the EPM that supplies the LWS, which is indicated by DTC (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. Disconnect first the lining wear sensor from EPM where the DTC points on. Measure the lining wear sensor supply externally with lining wear sensor supply deactivated. The voltage must be below 0.5V. Repeat for each LWS that is connected to the corresponding EPM. If not replace EPM. Activate the lining wear supply and the value shall be within 4.5-5.5V. If not replace EPM. Disconnect also EPM from central ECU. Check resistance between voltage supply pin of wire to EPM and wire to lining wear sensor supply. If resistance is smaller than 200 kOhm then error is in the wiring.', 'Wheel 10 Brake Lining Wear Supply Circuit'),
(1507, 'xBS', 'C105224', 'Sensor signal > 0.5V', 'Signal Stuck High', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors from all LWS that are connected to the EPM that supplies the LWS which is indicated by DTC (including check for chafing damage) for short circuits. Disconnect first the lining wear sensor from EPM where the DTC points on. Measure the lining wear sensor supply externally with lining wear sensor supply deactivated and the voltage must be below 0.5V. Repeat for each LWS that is connected to the corresponding EPM. If not replace EPM. Activate the lining wear supply and the value shall be within 4.5-5.5V. If not replace EPM. Disconnect also EPM from central ECU. Check resistance between voltage supply pin of wire to EPM and wire to lining wear sensor supply. If resistance is smaller than 200 kOhm then error is in the wiring.', 'Wheel 10 Brake Lining Wear Supply Circuit'),
(1508, 'xBS', 'U001088', 'ECU CAN controller in bus off.', 'Bus off', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - ECU damaged - Other ECU damaged connected to Backbone 1 network', 'Check the cables and connectors and wiring nodes between other backbone ECUs and central ECU. Check for sufficient power supply. If no fault found, check if no disturbing improper devices are mounted. If error still active check with other backbone ECUs. If error still active check with other central ECU.', 'CAN Communication Backbone 1 Net'),
(1509, 'xBS', 'U200768', 'EBS on Trailer request red warning', 'Event Information', NULL, '- Trailer ECU damaged - Low pressure on trailer - Low voltage on trailer', 'Check the fault memory of trailer EBS ECU(s).', 'CAN Communication Brake Proprietary Net'),
(1510, 'xBS', 'U200788', 'CAN controller in bus off, and change to one wire mode was not successful.', 'Bus off', NULL, 'Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) (incl. connection between truck and trailer)', 'Check if cables and connectors of ISO 11992 network are ok. Short circuit of both CAN wires, dirt or water in the connectors.', 'CAN Communication Brake Proprietary Net'),
(1511, 'xBS', 'U115387', 'Lost communication with ECU HMIIOM.', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting HMIIOM signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With HMIIOM'),
(1512, 'xBS', 'U115487', 'Lost communication with ECU BBM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Check for correct EOL configuration regarding BBM signals. If configuration is correct, then failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting BBM signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With BBM'),
(1513, 'xBS', 'U115587', 'Lost communication with ECU CIOM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting CIOM signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With CIOM'),
(1514, 'xBS', 'U115687', 'Lost communication with ECU RCIOM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting RCIOM signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With RCIOM'),
(1515, 'xBS', 'U115787', 'Lost communication with ECU CCIOM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting CCIOM signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With CCIOM'),
(1516, 'xBS', 'U115287', 'Lost communication with ECU ACM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting RECU signals (ACM or TECU) and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With RECU'),
(1517, 'xBS', 'U115887', 'Lost communication with ECU DACU', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Check for correct EOL configuration regarding DACU signals. If configuration is correct, then failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting DACU signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With DACU'),
(1518, 'xBS', 'U114887', 'Lost communication with the EPM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors and wiring nodes between EPMs and central ECU. Check for sufficient (UB+- 3V) power supply on the EPM. If same communication problem on other EPM. Try to remove EPMs one by one to detect the a faulty EPM. If the problem remains the problem is in the harness or ECU.', 'Wheel 1 Brake CAN Net'),
(1519, 'xBS', 'U114888', 'EPM CAN controller in bus off', 'Bus off', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Disconnect the EPM and check if faultcode is still active. - If active check shortcut between EPM supply and CAN High and Low. - If inactive replace EPM.', 'Wheel 1 Brake CAN Net'),
(1520, 'xBS', 'U114987', 'Lost communication with the EPM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors and wiring nodes between EPMs and central ECU. Check for sufficient (UB+- 3V) power supply on the EPM. If same communication problem on other EPM. Try to remove EPMs one by one to detect the a faulty EPM. If the problem remains the problem is in the harness or ECU.', 'Wheel 2 brake CAN Net'),
(1521, 'xBS', 'U114988', 'EPM CAN controller in bus off', 'Bus off', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Disconnect the EPM and check if faultcode is still active. - If active check shortcut between EPM supply and CAN High and Low. - If inactive replace EPM.', 'Wheel 2 brake CAN Net'),
(1522, 'xBS', 'U010087', 'Lost communication with ECU EMS', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting EMS signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication with EMS'),
(1523, 'xBS', 'U010187', 'Lost communication with ECU TECU', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Check for correct EOL configuration regarding signals of TECU. If configuration is correct, then failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting TECU signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication with TECU'),
(1524, 'xBS', 'U114087', 'Lost communication with ECU APM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Damaged sending ECU', 'Failure is out of EBS system. Check ECU:s transmitting APM signals and connected components.', 'Lost Communication With APM'),
(1525, 'xBS', 'U114A87', 'Lost communication with the EPM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors and wiring nodes between EPMs and central ECU. Check for sufficient (UB+- 3V) power supply on the EPM. If same communication problem on other EPM. Try to remove EPMs one by one to detect the a faulty EPM. If the problem remains the problem is in the harness or ECU.', 'Wheel 3 brake CAN Net'),
(1526, 'xBS', 'U114A88', 'EPM CAN controller in bus off', 'Bus off', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Disconnect the EPM and check if faultcode is still active. - If active check shortcut between EPM supply and CAN High and Low. - If inactive replace EPM.', 'Wheel 3 brake CAN Net'),
(1527, 'xBS', 'U114B87', 'Lost communication with the EPM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors and wiring nodes between EPMs and central ECU. Check for sufficient (UB+- 3V) power supply on the EPM. If same communication problem on other EPM. Try to remove EPMs one by one to detect the a faulty EPM. If the problem remains the problem is in the harness or ECU.', 'Wheel 4 brake CAN Net'),
(1528, 'xBS', 'U114B88', 'EPM CAN controller in bus off', 'Bus off', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Disconnect the EPM and check if faultcode is still active. - If active check shortcut between EPM supply and CAN High and Low. - If inactive replace EPM.', 'Wheel 4 brake CAN Net'),
(1529, 'xBS', 'U114C87', 'Lost communication with the EPM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors and wiring nodes between EPMs and central ECU. Check for sufficient (UB+- 3V) power supply on the EPM. If same communication problem on other EPM. Try to remove EPMs one by one to detect the a faulty EPM. If the problem remains the problem is in the harness or ECU.', 'Wheel 5 brake CAN Net'),
(1530, 'xBS', 'U114C88', 'EPM CAN controller in bus off', 'Bus off', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Disconnect the EPM and check if faultcode is still active. - If active check shortcut between EPM supply and CAN High and Low. - If inactive replace EPM.', 'Wheel 5 brake CAN Net');
