(1538, 'xBS', 'U115088', 'EPM CAN controller in bus off', 'Bus off', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Disconnect the EPM and check if faultcode is still active. - If active check shortcut between EPM supply and CAN High and Low. - If inactive replace EPM.', 'Wheel 9 brake CAN Net'),
(1539, 'xBS', 'U115187', 'Lost communication with the EPM', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors and wiring nodes between EPMs and central ECU. Check for sufficient (UB+- 3V) power supply on the EPM. If same communication problem on other EPM. Try to remove EPMs one by one to detect the a faulty EPM. If the problem remains the problem is in the harness or ECU.', 'Wheel 10 brake CAN Net'),
(1540, 'xBS', 'U115188', 'EPM CAN controller in bus off', 'Bus off', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - EPM damaged - ECU damaged', 'Disconnect the EPM and check if faultcode is still active. - If active check shortcut between EPM supply and CAN High and Low. - If inactive replace EPM.', 'Wheel 10 brake CAN Net'),
(1541, 'xBS', 'C005162', 'Sensor signal is implausible compared to yaw rate sensor signal and reference yaw rate.', 'Signal Compare Failure', NULL, '- Sensor is incorrectly calibrated - Drive of the sensor defect - Incorrect mounting - Steering system does not correspond to the vehicle specification (wrong steering gearbox or steering gear arm) - Sensor damaged - Wheelbase or wheeltrack do not correspond to the vehicle specification - Calibrated vehicle speed does not correspond to the wheel speeds', 'Check if sensor is calibrated correctly: with engine running, set steered wheels in straight position, read steering angle via diagnosis, check if the value of steering angle is 0 +- 10 degrees. If value is not OK, recalibrate the sensor. While engine still running, mark zero position on the steering wheel and turn it in both directions by one turn (360 degrees). Check the steering angle values via diagnosis (+-360 +-10 degrees). If values are not OK, check the mounting and the drive of the sensor. If fault is still active check steering system for specified parts (e.g. steering lever). With engine running turn the steering wheel to its end positions, read the steering angle values via diagnosis and check if the read values are within the allowed range defined in the dataset. If fault is still active, replace the steering angle sensor. Check whether wheelbase and wheeltrack correspond to the vehicle specification in the dataset and download correct dataset. Check for correct tacho signal calibration. If fault is still active replace the yaw rate sensor.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor'),
(1542, 'xBS', 'C006322', 'Sensor signal > range of the yaw-rate sensor.', 'Signal Amplitude Greater Than Maximum', NULL, '- Incorrect mounting - Sensor damaged', 'Check the mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU. If mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU is OK and the fault is still active, If the fault is still active, replace the yaw rate sensor/central ECU.', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1543, 'xBS', 'C006327', 'Sensor signal changed too fast.', 'Signal Rate of Change Above Threshold', NULL, '- Incorrect mounting - Sensor damaged', 'Check the mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU. If mounting of the sensor is OK and the fault is still active, replace the yaw rate sensor/central ECU.', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1544, 'xBS', 'C00632F', 'Noise, vibrations or implausible frequencies on the yaw rate sensor signal are detected by the central ECU.', 'Signal Erratic', NULL, '- Incorrect mounting - Sensor damaged', 'Check the mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU. If mounting of the sensor is OK and the fault is still active, replace the yaw rate sensor/central ECU.', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1545, 'xBS', 'C006349', 'Internal fault received from sensor via Sensor CAN', 'Internal Electronic Failure', NULL, 'Sensor damaged', 'Change the sensor', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1546, 'xBS', 'C00634A', 'The failure is detected if either iYRS is configured but not populated (according HW coding), or ext YRS is configured but ESP sensor CAN or ESP sensor supply is not populated.', 'Incorrect Component Installed', NULL, '- ECU hardware type. - Wrong dataset', 'Check if configuration matches the installation/central ECU type. Download correct dataset to Central ECU. Use correct part number of central ECU.', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1547, 'xBS', 'C006355', 'Sensor is detected, but not configured.', 'Not Configured', NULL, 'Installed but not configured component', 'Check if configuration matches installation. Download correct dataset.', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1548, 'xBS', 'C006364', 'Sensor signal is implausible compared to steering angle sensor signal and/or reference yaw rate.', 'Signal Plausibility Failure', NULL, '- Incorrect mounting - Sensor damaged - Wheelbase or wheeltrack do not correspond to the vehicle specification - Calibrated vehicle speed does not correspond to the wheel speeds', 'Check the mounting of the sensor. If the fault is still active check replace YRS/ECU.', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1549, 'xBS', 'C006376', 'Sign of the Sensor signal is incorrect.', 'Wrong Mounting Position', NULL, '- Incorrect mounting - Sensor damaged', 'Check the mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU. If mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU is OK and the fault is still active, calibrate the yaw rate sensor. If the fault is still active, replace the yaw rate sensor/central ECU.', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1550, 'xBS', 'C006392', '- Difference between measured and reference lateral acceleration is > 2 m/s^2. - Temporary error Flag is read from sensor CAN sent by yaw rate sensor', 'Performance or Incorrect Operation', NULL, 'See other reported ESP related faults', 'Check for other ESP-related faults.', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1551, 'xBS', 'C006396', 'Offset of sensor signal is too high.', 'Component Internal Failure', NULL, '- Conditions of calibration are not met - Incorrect mounting - Sensor damaged', 'Check and correct the mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU. If fault is still active, replace the yaw rate sensor/central ECU.', 'Yaw Rate Sensor'),
(1552, 'xBS', 'C006122', 'Sensor signal > 15 m/s^2', 'Signal Amplitude Greater Than Maximum', NULL, '- Incorrect mounting - Sensor damaged', 'Check the mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU. If the DTC counter is below 3, recalibrate the sensor. If the DTC counter is higher then 2, replace the yaw rate sensor/central ECU.', 'Lateral Acceleration Sensor'),
(1553, 'xBS', 'C006128', 'Sensor signal offset > 2.5 m/s^2', 'Signal Bias Level Out of Range / Zero Adjustment Failure', NULL, '- Incorrect mounting - Sensor damaged', 'Check the mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU. If mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU is OK and the fault is still active, calibrate the yaw rate sensor/central ECU. If fault is still active, replace the yaw rate sensor/central ECU.', 'Lateral Acceleration Sensor'),
(1554, 'xBS', 'C006154', 'Sensor not calibrated', 'Missing Calibration', NULL, 'Sensor not calibrated', 'Recalibrate the lateral acceleration sensor', 'Lateral Acceleration Sensor'),
(1555, 'xBS', 'C006164', 'Sensor signal is implausible compared to other ESP sensor signals and the reference yaw rate.', 'Signal Plausibility Failure', NULL, '- Sensor is incorrectly calibrated - Incorrect mounting - Steering system does not correspond to the vehicle specification (wrong steering gearbox or steering gear arm) - Sensor damaged - Wheelbase or wheeltrack do not correspond to the vehicle specification - Calibrated vehicle speed does not correspond to the wheel speeds', 'Check the mounting of the yaw rate sensor/central ECU. Perform standstill calibration. Check whether wheelbase and wheeltrack correspond to the vehicle specification and are correct programmed in the dataset, if necessary. Check calibration of vehicle speed. Check if sensor is calibrated correctly: with engine running, set steered wheels in straight position, read steering angle via diagnosis, check if the value of steering angle is 0 +- 10 degrees. If value is not OK, recalibrate the sensor. While engine still running, mark zero position on the steering wheel and turn it in both directions by one turn (360 degrees). Check the steering angle values via diagnosis (+-360 degrees). If values are not OK, check the mounting and the drive of the sensor. If fault is still active check steering system for specified parts (e.g. steering lever). With engine running turn the steering wheel to its end positions, read the steering angle values via diagnosis and check if the read values are within the allowed range defined in the dataset. If fault is still active, replace the yaw rate sensor/central ECU.', 'Lateral Acceleration Sensor'),
(1556, 'xBS', 'U012787', 'No CAN messages recevied from the sensor.', 'Missing Message', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - ECU damaged', 'Check the wiring and connectors between external yaw rate sensor and central ECU and between steering angle sensor and central ECU for open circuit and physical damage (including check for chafing damage), check the power supply of the ESP sensors 8,3V - 14,5V, if error still active, replace external yaw rate sensor, if error still active, replace central ECU.', 'Lost Communication With External Yaw Rate Sensor Module'),
(1557, 'xBS', 'C100D01', 'Voltage between EPM GND and wheel speed sensor (any pin) < 0,5V or > 4.3V.', 'General Electrical Failure', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Disconnect wheel speed sensor from EPM. 1. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. -> Change Sensor or wiring if out of range 2. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. -> Change Sensor or wiring if out of range 3. Connect the WSS, Measure Voltage between EPM GND and wheel speed sensor (any pin) Voltage must be between 0,5 - 4.3V. -> If it is in this range and error is still active, replace the EPM. 4. If it is out of range ( Below 0,5 or above 4.3 V ) , change sensor and or wiring. 5. If the faultcode is still active, change the EPM.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 1'),
(1558, 'xBS', 'C100D31', 'Implausible drop of signal (signal is frequently jumping between above 11 km/h and zero)', 'No Signal', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits (between H and L) and open-circuits. Measure Voltage between EPM GND and wheel speed sensor (any pin) Voltage must in range 0.5-4.3V. Disconnect wheel speed sensor from EPM. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h). Switch left/right WSS (with brakeout box) and see if the problem remain on the same side (vehicle has to be driven) =>replace EPM. If problem move to other side change defect sensor', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 1'),
(1559, 'xBS', 'C100D38', '- Plausibility test for the wheel speed sensor signal frequency - Rate of the ABS active/inactive status change is too high.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, '- Large airgap - Sensor or mounting damaged - Dirty or damaged tone wheel - Toggling tone wheel, production-failures of tone wheel', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Do waveform check with oscilloscope. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h). Check wheel speed sensor mounting (Check Klämhylsa). Check the tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 1'),
(1560, 'xBS', 'C100D3A', 'Minimum measurable wheel- speed >10 km/h', 'Signal Has Too Many Pulses', NULL, '- Large airgap - Dirty or damaged tone wheel - Toggling tone wheel, production-failures of tone wheel', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Do waveform check with oscilloscope. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h). Check wheel speed sensor mounting (Check Klämhylsa). Check the tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 1'),
(1561, 'xBS', 'C100D54', 'Difference between the learned wheel circumferences and programmed values > 25%', 'Missing Calibration', NULL, '- Tyre with wrong circumference is mounted on one of the axels - Tachograph not calibrated - Wrong number of teeth of tone wheel.', 'Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3- 4km/h). Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. If possible : Check tone wheel by checking wheel speed sensor signal for correct wave(Not possible to define the correct waveform) form according the specification for wheel speed sensor wave form or check tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth. Check wheel speed sensor mounting.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 1'),
(1562, 'xBS', 'C100D55', 'Sensor is detected, but not configured.', 'Not Configured', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) (dirt in the connector ,low resistance detected)) - Connected but not correctly configured sensor - Sensor connected to incorrect EPM connector', 'Check if configuration matches installation. Check if sensor connected according to wiring diagram. If configuration matches installation, check wheel speed sensors connector of EPM', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 1'),
(1563, 'xBS', 'C100D95', 'Shortcut between sensors connected to the same EPM', 'Incorrect Assembly', NULL, 'Damaged wire(s) or connector(s)', 'Disconnect wheel speed sensor from EPM. Measure resistance between all connected sensor in pairs. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Replace sensors or harness', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 1'),
(1564, 'xBS', 'C100E01', 'Voltage between EPM GND and wheel speed sensor (any pin) < 0,5V or > 4.3V.', 'General Electrical Failure', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor damaged - EPM damaged', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Disconnect wheel speed sensor from EPM. 1. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. -> Change Sensor or wiring if out of range 2. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. -> Change Sensor or wiring if out of range 3. Connect the WSS, Measure Voltage between EPM GND and wheel speed sensor (any pin) Voltage must be between 0,5 - 4.3V. -> If it is in this range and error is still active, replace the EPM. 4. If it is out of range ( Below 0,5 or above 4.3 V ) , change sensor and or wiring. 5. If the faultcode is still active, change the EPM.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 2'),
(1565, 'xBS', 'C100E31', 'Implausible drop of signal (signal is frequently jumping between above 11 km/h and zero)', 'No Signal', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor or mounting damaged - EPM damaged - Too large airgap between tone wheel and sensor', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits (between H and L) and open-circuits. Measure Voltage between EPM GND and wheel speed sensor (any pin) Voltage must in range 0.5-4.3V. Disconnect wheel speed sensor from EPM. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h). Switch left/right WSS (with brakeout box) and see if the problem remain on the same side (vehicle has to be driven) =>replace EPM. If problem move to other side change defect sensor', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 2'),
(1566, 'xBS', 'C100E38', '- Plausibility test for the wheel speed sensor signal frequency - Rate of the ABS active/inactive status change is too high.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, '- Large airgap - Sensor or mounting damaged - Dirty or damaged tone wheel - Toggling tone wheel, production-failures of tone wheel', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Do waveform check with oscilloscope. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h). Check wheel speed sensor mounting (Check Klämhylsa). Check the tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 2'),
(1567, 'xBS', 'C100E3A', 'Minimum measurable wheel- speed >10 km/h', 'Signal Has Too Many Pulses', NULL, '- Large airgap - Dirty or damaged tone wheel - Toggling tone wheel, production-failures of tone wheel', 'Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3- 4km/h). Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. If possible : Check tone wheel by checking wheel speed sensor signal for correct wave(Not possible to define the correct waveform) form according the specification for wheel speed sensor wave form or check tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth. Check wheel speed sensor mounting.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 2'),
(1568, 'xBS', 'C100E54', 'Difference between the learned wheel circumferences and programmed values > 25%', 'Missing Calibration', NULL, '- Tyre with wrong circumference is mounted on one of the axels - Tachograph not calibrated - Wrong number of teeth of tone wheel.', 'Check if tire size of all tires is according vehicle specification. Check C3 Signal calibration, check tachograp for additional faultcodes. Check number of teeth on tone wheel on all wheels. (Check tire size of all tires in data set.) V3P to check', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 2'),
(1569, 'xBS', 'C100E55', 'Sensor is detected, but not configured.', 'Not Configured', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) (dirt in the connector ,low resistance detected)) - Connected but not correctly configured sensor - Sensor connected to incorrect EPM connector', 'Check if configuration matches installation. Check if sensor connected according to wiring diagram. If configuration matches installation, check wheel speed sensors connector of EPM', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 2'),
