(1600, 'xBS', 'C101331', 'Implausible drop of signal (signal is frequently jumping between above 11 km/h and zero)', 'No Signal', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) - Sensor or mounting damaged - EPM damaged - Too large airgap between tone wheel and sensor', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits (between H and L) and open-circuits. Measure Voltage between EPM GND and wheel speed sensor (any pin) Voltage must in range 0.5-4.3V. Disconnect wheel speed sensor from EPM. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h). Switch left/right WSS (with brakeout box) and see if the problem remain on the same side (vehicle has to be driven) =>replace EPM. If problem move to other side change defect sensor', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 7'),
(1601, 'xBS', 'C101338', '- Plausibility test for the wheel speed sensor signal frequency - Rate of the ABS active/inactive status change is too high.', 'Signal Frequency Incorrect', NULL, '- Large airgap - Sensor or mounting damaged - Dirty or damaged tone wheel - Toggling tone wheel, production-failures of tone wheel', 'Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. Do waveform check with oscilloscope. Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3-5km/h). Check wheel speed sensor mounting (Check Klämhylsa). Check the tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 7');
INSERT INTO `dtc_list` (`id`, `node`, `dtc_iso`, `failure_event`, `ftb_name`, `funct_behavior_desc`, `possible_root_cause`, `workshop_action`, `proprietary_name`) VALUES
(1602, 'xBS', 'C10133A', 'Minimum measurable wheel- speed >10 km/h', 'Signal Has Too Many Pulses', NULL, '- Large airgap - Dirty or damaged tone wheel - Toggling tone wheel, production-failures of tone wheel', 'Check and correct air gap between wheel speed sensor and tone wheel by measuring the wheel speed signal. (Wheel speed sensor signal must be higher than 100mV peak to peak at wheel speed of about 3- 4km/h). Check the cables and connectors between EPM and wheel-speed sensor for short-circuits and open-circuits. Measure resistance of Sensor and cabling. Resistance must be between 800 …. 2000 Ohm. Measure insulation resistance of sensor and cabling to vehicle GND. Resistance must be > 200kOhm. If possible : Check tone wheel by checking wheel speed sensor signal for correct wave(Not possible to define the correct waveform) form according the specification for wheel speed sensor wave form or check tone wheel for dirt and metallic particles, for wobble, for pitch error, for the correct number of teeth. Check wheel speed sensor mounting.', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 7'),
(1603, 'xBS', 'C101354', 'Difference between the learned wheel circumferences and programmed values > 25%', 'Missing Calibration', NULL, '- Tyre with wrong circumference is mounted on one of the axels - Tachograph not calibrated - Wrong number of teeth of tone wheel.', 'Check if tire size of all tires is according vehicle specification. Check C3 Signal calibration, check tachograp for additional faultcodes. Check number of teeth on tone wheel on all wheels. (Check tire size of all tires in data set.) V3P to check', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 7'),
(1604, 'xBS', 'C101355', 'Sensor is detected, but not configured.', 'Not Configured', NULL, '- Damaged wire(s) or connector(s) (dirt in the connector ,low resistance detected)) - Connected but not correctly configured sensor - Sensor connected to incorrect EPM connector', 'Check if configuration matches installation. Check if sensor connected according to wiring diagram. If configuration matches installation, check wheel speed sensors connector of EPM', 'Wheel Speed Sensor 7'),
